window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 27 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070581","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If A @ B &#8594; A is added to B<br>A &#9733; B &#8594; A is multiplied by B<br>A # B &#8594; A is divided by B<br>A &#36; B &#8594; B is subtracted from A<br>Then: (1825 # 15) &#36; (137 # 3) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि A @ B &#8594; A में B जोड़ा जाता है<br>A &#9733; B &#8594; A को B से गुणा किया जाता है<br>A # B &#8594; A को B से भाग दिया जाता है<br>A &#36; B &#8594; A में से B घटाया जाता है<br>तब: (1825 # 15) &#36; (137 # 3) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"76"},"2":{"en":"90"},"3":{"en":"56"},"4":{"en":"29"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"1825 # 15 means 1825 is divided by 15 and 137 # 3 means 137 is divided by 3<br>The sign &#36; means the second value is subtracted from the first, so the value is 1825/15 − 137/3<br>Taking a common denominator of 15: 1825/15 − 685/15 = 1140/15 = 76<br>So the value of the expression is 76<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 76.</b>","hi":"1825 # 15 का अर्थ 1825 में 15 से भाग तथा 137 # 3 का अर्थ 137 में 3 से भाग है<br>&#36; का अर्थ पहले मान में से दूसरा मान घटाना है, अतः मान 1825/15 − 137/3 है<br>15 का समान हर लेने पर: 1825/15 − 685/15 = 1140/15 = 76<br>अतः व्यंजक का मान 76 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 76 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070582","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If + = ÷, − = +, × = −, ÷ = ×, then which of the following is correct? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि + = ÷, − = +, × = −, ÷ = × है, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सही है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"144 + 12 − 4 × 12 = 4"},"2":{"en":"244 ÷ 42 + 21 − 10 = 120"},"3":{"en":"100 × 30 − 42 + 20 = 1000"},"4":{"en":"168 − 81 × 25 + 40 = 100"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Replacing the signs in the first equation: 144 ÷ 12 + 4 − 12 = 12 + 4 − 12 = 4 ✔<br>In the second equation 244 × 42 ÷ 21 + 10 = 488 + 10 = 498, not 120; in the third 100 − 30 + 42 ÷ 20 = 72.1, not 1000 and in the fourth 168 + 81 − 25 ÷ 40 = 248.375, not 100<br>So only the first equation is correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 144 + 12 − 4 × 12 = 4.</b>","hi":"पहले समीकरण में चिह्न बदलने पर 144 ÷ 12 + 4 − 12 = 12 + 4 − 12 = 4 ✔<br>दूसरे समीकरण में 244 × 42 ÷ 21 + 10 = 498 है, 120 नहीं; तीसरे में 100 − 30 + 42 ÷ 20 = 72.1 है, 1000 नहीं तथा चौथे में 168 + 81 − 25 ÷ 40 = 248.375 है, 100 नहीं<br>अतः केवल पहला समीकरण सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 144 + 12 − 4 × 12 = 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070583","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What is the sum of 34, 26, and 40? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"34, 26 तथा 40 का योग क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"110"},"2":{"en":"90"},"3":{"en":"80"},"4":{"en":"100"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"34 + 26 = 60 and 60 + 40 = 100<br>So the sum is 100<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 100.</b>","hi":"34 + 26 = 60 तथा 60 + 40 = 100<br>अतः योग 100 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 100 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070584","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Directions: Select the pair that represents exactly the relation expressed in the given pair.<br>Scissors : Cut :: Broom : ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निर्देश: वह युग्म चुनिए जो दिए गए युग्म में व्यक्त संबंध को ठीक वैसे ही दर्शाता है।<br>Scissors : Cut :: Broom : ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sweep"},"2":{"en":"Hit"},"3":{"en":"Crush"},"4":{"en":"Slice"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A pair of scissors is the tool used to cut, so the pair shows a tool and the work it does<br>A broom is the tool used to sweep, which is the same tool and its work<br>Hitting, crushing and slicing are done by other tools<br>Hence the answer is Sweep<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Sweep.</b>","hi":"कैंची वह उपकरण है जिससे काटा जाता है, अतः युग्म उपकरण और उसके कार्य का संबंध दर्शाता है<br>झाड़ू वह उपकरण है जिससे बुहारा जाता है, जो वही उपकरण-कार्य संबंध है<br>मारना, कुचलना तथा टुकड़े करना अन्य उपकरणों से होता है<br>अतः उत्तर Sweep है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Sweep है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070585","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dictionary / Alphabetical Order","question":{"en":"Identify the word that comes first in a dictionary. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह शब्द पहचानिए जो शब्दकोश में पहले आता है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Abandon"},"2":{"en":"Abstract"},"3":{"en":"Ability"},"4":{"en":"Absolute"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"All four words begin with the letters A b, so the third letter decides the order<br>The third letters are a in Abandon, s in Abstract, i in Ability and s in Absolute<br>A comes first, so Abandon comes first in the dictionary<br>Hence Abandon is the answer<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Abandon.</b>","hi":"चारों शब्द A b से शुरू होते हैं, अतः तीसरा अक्षर क्रम निर्धारित करता है<br>तीसरे अक्षर हैं Abandon में a, Abstract में s, Ability में i तथा Absolute में s<br>a सबसे पहले आता है, अतः शब्दकोश में Abandon पहले आएगा<br>इसलिए उत्तर Abandon है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Abandon है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070586","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"If some cities are crowded and all crowded places are polluted, what conclusion logically follows? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि कुछ शहर भीड़भाड़ वाले हैं और सभी भीड़भाड़ वाले स्थान प्रदूषित हैं, तो तार्किक रूप से कौन-सा निष्कर्ष निकलता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Some cities are polluted","hi":"कुछ शहर प्रदूषित हैं"},"2":{"en":"All cities are polluted","hi":"सभी शहर प्रदूषित हैं"},"3":{"en":"All polluted places are cities","hi":"सभी प्रदूषित स्थान शहर हैं"},"4":{"en":"No city is polluted","hi":"कोई शहर प्रदूषित नहीं है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Some cities are crowded and every crowded place is polluted, so those crowded cities fall inside the polluted group<br>That gives some cities which are polluted<br>The other options either make the statement universal or reverse the relation, so they do not follow<br>Hence some cities are polluted<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Some cities are polluted.</b>","hi":"कुछ शहर भीड़भाड़ वाले हैं और प्रत्येक भीड़भाड़ वाला स्थान प्रदूषित है, अतः वे भीड़भाड़ वाले शहर प्रदूषित समूह के भीतर आते हैं<br>इससे कुछ शहर प्रदूषित निकलते हैं<br>अन्य विकल्प कथन को सार्वभौमिक बना देते हैं या संबंध उलट देते हैं, अतः वे नहीं निकलते<br>इसलिए कुछ शहर प्रदूषित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): कुछ शहर प्रदूषित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070587","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In Image X, look at the first set of figures. The first and second figures are related in a certain way. For the second pair, choose the missing figure from Image Y's options using the same relationship.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"Image X में आकृतियों के पहले समूह को देखिए। पहली और दूसरी आकृति का आपस में एक निश्चित संबंध है। दूसरे युग्म के लिए उसी संबंध का प्रयोग करते हुए Image Y के विकल्पों में से लुप्त आकृति चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first pair a plain circle becomes the same circle divided into eight equal sectors by four lines drawn through its centre<br>So the relation is: the shape is kept and divided into eight equal parts by lines passing through the centre<br>For the second pair the rhombus must be kept and divided into eight equal parts by its two diagonals together with the vertical and horizontal lines through its centre<br>Only the figure of option 4 shows the rhombus cut into eight equal parts in this way, so the fourth option completes the pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में सादा वृत्त वही वृत्त बन जाता है जो केंद्र से गुजरने वाली चार रेखाओं से आठ बराबर भागों में विभाजित है<br>अतः संबंध है: आकृति को वैसा ही रखकर केंद्र से गुजरने वाली रेखाओं से आठ बराबर भागों में बाँटना<br>दूसरे युग्म में समचतुर्भुज को वैसा ही रखकर उसके दो विकर्णों तथा केंद्र से गुजरने वाली ऊर्ध्व और क्षैतिज रेखाओं से आठ बराबर भागों में बाँटना है<br>केवल विकल्प 4 की आकृति में समचतुर्भुज इस प्रकार आठ बराबर भागों में विभाजित है, अतः चौथा विकल्प युग्म पूरा करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070588","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Given that # means subtract and &#9733; means add, find the result of 12 &#9733; 5 # 7. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि # का अर्थ घटाना तथा &#9733; का अर्थ जोड़ना है, तो 12 &#9733; 5 # 7 का परिणाम ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"14"},"3":{"en":"17"},"4":{"en":"20"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Replacing the signs, the expression becomes 12 + 5 − 7<br>12 + 5 = 17 and 17 − 7 = 10<br>So the result is 10<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 10.</b>","hi":"चिह्न बदलने पर व्यंजक 12 + 5 − 7 बनता है<br>12 + 5 = 17 तथा 17 − 7 = 10<br>अतः परिणाम 10 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070589","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Which Venn diagram best represents the relationship among Men, Fathers, and Pilots?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा वेन आरेख Men, Fathers तथा Pilots के बीच संबंध सर्वोत्तम दर्शाता है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every father is a man, so the circle of fathers lies completely inside the circle of men<br>Pilots may be men or women, so the circle of pilots cuts across the circle of men and only a part of it lies inside men<br>Diagram 2 shows one small circle inside a big circle and a third circle overlapping the big one, which matches this<br>Hence the second diagram is the correct one<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पिता पुरुष है, अतः पिताओं का वृत्त पुरुषों के वृत्त के पूरी तरह भीतर है<br>पायलट पुरुष या महिला हो सकते हैं, अतः पायलटों का वृत्त पुरुषों के वृत्त को काटता है और उसका केवल एक भाग पुरुषों के भीतर है<br>आरेख 2 में एक छोटा वृत्त बड़े वृत्त के भीतर और तीसरा वृत्त बड़े वृत्त को काटता हुआ है, जो इसी से मेल खाता है<br>अतः दूसरा आरेख सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9.jpg"]}},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070590","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Select the figure in Image Y that accurately shows the right-side mirror reflection of Image X.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"Image Y में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो Image X का दाईं ओर से दर्पण प्रतिबिंब ठीक प्रकार दर्शाती है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Image X has four corner arrows pointing outward and eight small triangles around the centre, with the shaded triangles alternating on the two sides<br>In a mirror placed on the right side the left and right parts interchange while up and down stay the same, so every shaded triangle must move to the other side and the corner arrows must keep pointing outward<br>Option 2 shows exactly this arrangement with the sides of the shaded triangles exchanged<br>Hence the second option is the correct mirror reflection<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"Image X में चारों कोनों पर बाहर की ओर संकेत करते तीर तथा केंद्र के चारों ओर आठ छोटे त्रिभुज हैं, जिनमें छायांकित त्रिभुज दोनों ओर बारी-बारी हैं<br>दाईं ओर रखे दर्पण में बायाँ-दायाँ भाग परस्पर बदल जाता है और ऊपर-नीचे वही रहता है, अतः प्रत्येक छायांकित त्रिभुज को दूसरी ओर आना चाहिए और कोनों के तीर बाहर की ओर ही रहने चाहिए<br>विकल्प 2 में छायांकित त्रिभुजों की भुजाएँ इसी प्रकार बदली हुई हैं<br>अतः दूसरा विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070591","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Identify the figure in Image Y that represents the folded appearance of the transparent sheet in Image X along the dotted line.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"Image Y में से वह आकृति पहचानिए जो Image X की पारदर्शी शीट को बिंदुदार रेखा के अनुदिश मोड़ने पर बनने वाला रूप दर्शाती है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The sheet is folded along the vertical dotted line that runs near its left edge, so the narrow left strip falls on the rest of the sheet<br>The curved leaf shape of the upper part is seen twice, once directly and once as its mirror copy through the sheet, and the small circle lying on the fold line stays a single circle on the fold<br>Option A shows the complete leaf formed by the two mirrored halves with the small circle on the fold, while the other options show only one half of the leaf or break the curve<br>Hence the figure in option 1 is the folded appearance<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"शीट को उस बिंदुदार ऊर्ध्व रेखा के अनुदिश मोड़ा जाता है जो उसके बाईं ओर के पास है, अतः बाईं पतली पट्टी शीट के बाकी भाग पर आ जाती है<br>ऊपरी भाग की वक्र पत्ती जैसी आकृति दो बार दिखती है, एक बार सीधी और एक बार शीट के भीतर से उसकी दर्पण प्रतिकृति के रूप में, तथा मोड़ रेखा पर पड़ा छोटा वृत्त मोड़ पर एक ही वृत्त रहता है<br>विकल्प A में दोनों दर्पण आधों से बनी पूरी पत्ती तथा मोड़ पर छोटा वृत्त दिखता है, जबकि अन्य विकल्पों में पत्ती का केवल एक आधा भाग है या वक्र टूट जाता है<br>अतः विकल्प 1 की आकृति मुड़ा हुआ रूप है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q10_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070592","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A series of registration codes is generated based on prime numbers. The code follows the format [Prime No.]-[Next Consecutive Prime No.]. Which code does not follow this rule? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पंजीकरण कूटों की एक श्रेणी अभाज्य संख्याओं पर आधारित है। कूट का प्रारूप [अभाज्य संख्या]-[अगली क्रमागत अभाज्य संख्या] है। कौन-सा कूट इस नियम का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13-17"},"2":{"en":"23-29"},"3":{"en":"31-37"},"4":{"en":"41-49"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The prime numbers after 13 is 17, after 23 is 29 and after 31 is 37, so the first three codes name a prime and the very next prime<br>After 41 the next prime is 43, but the code shows 49, and 49 = 7 × 7 is not a prime at all ✘<br>So 41-49 does not follow the rule<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 41-49.</b>","hi":"13 के बाद अभाज्य संख्या 17, 23 के बाद 29 तथा 31 के बाद 37 है, अतः पहले तीन कूट किसी अभाज्य संख्या और उसके ठीक बाद की अभाज्य संख्या को दर्शाते हैं<br>41 के बाद अगली अभाज्य संख्या 43 है, परंतु कूट में 49 है, और 49 = 7 × 7 अभाज्य ही नहीं है ✘<br>अतः 41-49 नियम का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 41-49 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070593","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You wake up to a furious, fully capitalised email sent at 2:00 AM by your CEO, demanding an immediate explanation for a minor &#8377;10,000 accounting discrepancy. To effectively \"manage upward,\" how do you respond to this emotionally volatile communication? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप सुबह उठते हैं और देखते हैं कि आपके CEO ने रात 2:00 बजे पूरे बड़े अक्षरों में एक क्रोधित ईमेल भेजा है, जिसमें 10,000 रुपये की छोटी लेखा विसंगति के लिए तत्काल स्पष्टीकरण माँगा गया है। इस भावनात्मक रूप से अस्थिर संवाद का प्रभावी ढंग से \"ऊपर की ओर प्रबंधन\" करने के लिए आप कैसे उत्तर देंगे? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reply immediately at 2:00 AM with a highly defensive explanation to clear your name instantly.","hi":"तुरंत अपना बचाव करने के लिए रात 2:00 बजे ही अत्यधिक रक्षात्मक उत्तर भेजना।"},"2":{"en":"Ignore the email permanently to teach the CEO a lesson about appropriate workplace boundaries.","hi":"उचित कार्यस्थल सीमाओं का पाठ पढ़ाने के लिए ईमेल को स्थायी रूप से अनदेखा करना।"},"3":{"en":"Wait until morning, acknowledge their urgency calmly, and provide a concise, factual report.","hi":"सुबह तक प्रतीक्षा करना, उनकी तात्कालिकता को शांति से स्वीकार करना और संक्षिप्त, तथ्यात्मक रिपोर्ट देना।"},"4":{"en":"Forward the CEO's angry email directly to the HR department to file an official formal grievance.","hi":"आधिकारिक औपचारिक शिकायत दर्ज कराने के लिए CEO का क्रोधित ईमेल सीधे मानव संसाधन विभाग को अग्रेषित करना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The CEO's anger is about a small accounting difference and needs facts, not emotion, so a defensive reply at 2 AM only deepens the conflict<br>Ignoring the mail or dragging HR into a small matter would damage the working relationship<br>Answering in the morning with a calm acknowledgement of the urgency and a short factual report gives the CEO exactly what is needed and keeps the exchange professional<br>So the third response manages upward most effectively<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Wait until morning, acknowledge their urgency calmly, and provide a concise, factual report.</b>","hi":"CEO का क्रोध छोटी लेखा भिन्नता के बारे में है और उसे तथ्य चाहिए, भावना नहीं, अतः रात 2 बजे रक्षात्मक उत्तर केवल टकराव बढ़ाता है<br>ईमेल अनदेखा करना या छोटी बात में मानव संसाधन को घसीटना कार्य संबंध को हानि पहुँचाएगा<br>सुबह शांतिपूर्वक तात्कालिकता स्वीकार करते हुए संक्षिप्त तथ्यात्मक रिपोर्ट देने से CEO को वही मिलता है जो आवश्यक है और संवाद पेशेवर बना रहता है<br>अतः तीसरा उत्तर ऊपर की ओर प्रबंधन सर्वाधिक प्रभावी ढंग से करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): सुबह तक प्रतीक्षा करना, उनकी तात्कालिकता को शांति से स्वीकार करना और संक्षिप्त, तथ्यात्मक रिपोर्ट देना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070594","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government has introduced additional buses on major routes to improve connectivity and reduce overcrowding during peak hours.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The government believes increasing bus services can improve public transport.<br>II. Private vehicles have been banned on major routes.<br>III. Overcrowding exists on some public transport routes. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार ने कनेक्टिविटी सुधारने तथा व्यस्त समय में भीड़ कम करने के लिए प्रमुख मार्गों पर अतिरिक्त बसें शुरू की हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सरकार मानती है कि बस सेवाएँ बढ़ाने से सार्वजनिक परिवहन बेहतर हो सकता है।<br>II. प्रमुख मार्गों पर निजी वाहनों पर प्रतिबंध लगा दिया गया है।<br>III. कुछ सार्वजनिक परिवहन मार्गों पर भीड़ है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और II निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only Inference III follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष III निकलता है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Adding buses to improve connectivity shows the belief that more bus service improves public transport, so I follows<br>The reason given for the extra buses is to reduce overcrowding during peak hours, which means overcrowding already exists on those routes, so III follows<br>Nothing is said about banning private vehicles, so II does not follow<br>Hence only inferences I and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only Inferences I and III follow.</b>","hi":"कनेक्टिविटी सुधारने के लिए बसें बढ़ाना यह विश्वास दर्शाता है कि अधिक बस सेवा से सार्वजनिक परिवहन बेहतर होता है, अतः I निकलता है<br>अतिरिक्त बसों का कारण व्यस्त समय में भीड़ कम करना बताया गया है, जिसका अर्थ है कि उन मार्गों पर भीड़ पहले से है, अतः III निकलता है<br>निजी वाहनों पर प्रतिबंध के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहा गया, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070595","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A national park has limited the number of daily visitors during the peak tourist season.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Tourism activities have caused irreversible damage throughout the entire park.<br>II. Visitor restrictions will completely eliminate environmental concerns in the park. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक राष्ट्रीय उद्यान ने पर्यटन के व्यस्त मौसम में दैनिक आगंतुकों की संख्या सीमित कर दी है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. पर्यटन गतिविधियों ने पूरे उद्यान में अपरिवर्तनीय क्षति पहुँचाई है।<br>II. आगंतुक प्रतिबंध उद्यान की पर्यावरणीय चिंताओं को पूरी तरह समाप्त कर देंगे। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Limiting visitors shows only that crowd pressure is a concern; it does not say that damage has already been done throughout the whole park, so conclusion I does not follow<br>Limiting the number of visitors can reduce pressure but can never remove all environmental concerns, so the word completely makes conclusion II too strong<br>Hence neither conclusion follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"आगंतुकों को सीमित करना केवल यह दर्शाता है कि भीड़ का दबाव चिंता का विषय है; यह नहीं कहता कि पूरे उद्यान में क्षति पहले ही हो चुकी है, अतः निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>आगंतुकों की संख्या सीमित करना दबाव घटा सकता है, परंतु सभी पर्यावरणीय चिंताएँ कभी नहीं हटा सकता, अतः 'पूरी तरह' शब्द निष्कर्ष II को अत्यधिक दृढ़ बना देता है<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070596","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Which strategy should a leader implement to establish a culture where employees feel safe offering honest feedback? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक नेता को ऐसी संस्कृति बनाने के लिए कौन-सी रणनीति अपनानी चाहिए जिसमें कर्मचारी ईमानदार प्रतिक्रिया देने में सुरक्षित महसूस करें? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Establish a strictly anonymous complaint box that is rarely addressed.","hi":"ऐसा गुमनाम शिकायत बॉक्स बनाना जिस पर शायद ही कार्रवाई होती हो।"},"2":{"en":"Actively encourage constructive disagreement while protecting employees from negative consequences.","hi":"रचनात्मक असहमति को सक्रिय रूप से प्रोत्साहित करना तथा कर्मचारियों को नकारात्मक परिणामों से सुरक्षा देना।"},"3":{"en":"Only ask for feedback during formal, annual performance reviews.","hi":"प्रतिक्रिया केवल औपचारिक वार्षिक प्रदर्शन समीक्षा के समय माँगना।"},"4":{"en":"Reward team members who never challenge management decisions.","hi":"ऐसे सदस्यों को पुरस्कृत करना जो प्रबंधन के निर्णयों पर कभी प्रश्न नहीं उठाते।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"People speak honestly only when they expect their words to be heard and to bring them no harm, so the leader must invite disagreement openly and guarantee protection from punishment<br>An ignored complaint box and feedback once a year give no such assurance, and rewarding silence teaches people to hide problems<br>So actively encouraging constructive disagreement while protecting employees is the right strategy<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Actively encourage constructive disagreement while protecting employees from negative consequences.</b>","hi":"लोग ईमानदारी से तभी बोलते हैं जब उन्हें विश्वास हो कि उनकी बात सुनी जाएगी और उससे उन्हें हानि नहीं होगी, अतः नेता को असहमति को खुलकर आमंत्रित करना चाहिए तथा दंड से सुरक्षा का भरोसा देना चाहिए<br>अनदेखा पड़ा शिकायत बॉक्स और वर्ष में एक बार प्रतिक्रिया ऐसा भरोसा नहीं देते, तथा चुप्पी को पुरस्कृत करने से लोग समस्याएँ छिपाना सीखते हैं<br>अतः रचनात्मक असहमति को सक्रिय रूप से प्रोत्साहित करना तथा सुरक्षा देना सही रणनीति है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): रचनात्मक असहमति को सक्रिय रूप से प्रोत्साहित करना तथा कर्मचारियों को नकारात्मक परिणामों से सुरक्षा देना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070597","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Direction:<br>Select the most appropriate decision.<br>A government agency must choose between funding a project with high expected benefits but uncertain outcomes and another with moderate benefits but highly predictable results. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निर्देश:<br>सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त निर्णय चुनिए।<br>एक सरकारी एजेंसी को ऐसे परियोजना को वित्त देने के बीच चुनना है जिसके अपेक्षित लाभ अधिक हैं परंतु परिणाम अनिश्चित हैं, तथा दूसरी परियोजना के बीच जिसके लाभ मध्यम हैं परंतु परिणाम अत्यधिक पूर्वानुमेय हैं। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Select the project with uncertain outcomes solely because benefits appear larger.","hi":"केवल इसलिए अनिश्चित परिणाम वाली परियोजना चुनना क्योंकि लाभ बड़े दिखते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Select the predictable project solely because uncertainty should be avoided.","hi":"केवल इसलिए पूर्वानुमेय परियोजना चुनना क्योंकि अनिश्चितता से बचना चाहिए।"},"3":{"en":"Evaluate expected impact, risk levels, and strategic priorities before deciding.","hi":"निर्णय लेने से पहले अपेक्षित प्रभाव, जोखिम स्तर तथा रणनीतिक प्राथमिकताओं का मूल्यांकन करना।"},"4":{"en":"Divide resources equally without considering differences in expected outcomes.","hi":"अपेक्षित परिणामों के अंतर पर विचार किए बिना संसाधन बराबर बाँट देना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Both projects have merit which depends on how large the expected gain is against how likely it is to come, and on which need the agency gives priority<br>Choosing on one reason alone ignores either the risk or the benefit, and splitting the money equally ignores both figures<br>Weighing the expected impact, the risk level and the strategic priorities gives a decision based on all the facts<br>So the third course of action is the most appropriate decision<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Evaluate expected impact, risk levels, and strategic priorities before deciding.</b>","hi":"दोनों परियोजनाओं का अपना महत्व है, जो इस पर निर्भर है कि अपेक्षित लाभ कितना बड़ा है उसके मिलने की संभावना कितनी है, तथा एजेंसी किस आवश्यकता को प्राथमिकता देती है<br>केवल एक कारण से चुनने पर या तो जोखिम या लाभ की उपेक्षा होती है, और धन बराबर बाँटने पर दोनों आँकड़े अनदेखे रह जाते हैं<br>अपेक्षित प्रभाव, जोखिम स्तर तथा रणनीतिक प्राथमिकताओं को तौलने से सभी तथ्यों पर आधारित निर्णय होता है<br>अतः तीसरा कार्यवाही-क्रम सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त निर्णय है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निर्णय लेने से पहले अपेक्षित प्रभाव, जोखिम स्तर तथा रणनीतिक प्राथमिकताओं का मूल्यांकन करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070598","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"The following diagram shows the number of children playing Basketball, Cricket, Football, and Volleyball.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]<br>If the total number of children is 600, what is the approximate percentage of children playing at least two games? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित आरेख में बास्केटबॉल, क्रिकेट, फुटबॉल तथा वॉलीबॉल खेलने वाले बच्चों की संख्या दर्शाई गई है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]<br>यदि बच्चों की कुल संख्या 600 है, तो कम से कम दो खेल खेलने वाले बच्चों का अनुमानित प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9.83%"},"2":{"en":"7.13%"},"3":{"en":"10.54%"},"4":{"en":"8.03%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The children playing at least two games are those counted in the overlapping parts of the diagram<br>Adding those parts: 14 + 11 + 6 + 7 + 9 + 12 = 59<br>So the required percentage is 59 ÷ 600 × 100 = 9.83%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 9.83%.</b>","hi":"कम से कम दो खेल खेलने वाले बच्चे आरेख के अतिव्यापी भागों में गिने जाते हैं<br>उन भागों को जोड़ने पर: 14 + 11 + 6 + 7 + 9 + 12 = 59<br>अतः अभीष्ट प्रतिशत 59 ÷ 600 × 100 = 9.83% है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 9.83% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070599","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Farmers are increasingly switching to solar-powered irrigation pumps because they are more cost-effective than diesel pumps in the long run.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Farmers value long-term cost-effectiveness when choosing their irrigation methods.<br>II. The high initial installation cost of solar pumps is a major barrier for all farmers. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित निम्नलिखित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>किसान सोलर चालित सिंचाई पंपों की ओर बढ़ रहे हैं क्योंकि लंबे समय में ये डीज़ल पंपों से अधिक लागत-कुशल हैं।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. सिंचाई के तरीके चुनते समय किसान दीर्घकालिक लागत-कुशलता को महत्व देते हैं।<br>II. सोलर पंपों की ऊँची प्रारंभिक स्थापना लागत सभी किसानों के लिए बड़ी बाधा है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Farmers are shifting to solar pumps because they cost less in the long run, which is possible only if farmers really care about long-term cost, so assumption I is implicit<br>The statement never mentions the initial cost of installation, and the word all would in any case make the claim too broad, so assumption II is not implicit<br>Hence only assumption I is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"किसान सोलर पंपों की ओर इसलिए बढ़ रहे हैं क्योंकि लंबे समय में उनकी लागत कम है, जो तभी संभव है जब किसान दीर्घकालिक लागत को महत्व दें, अतः अवधारणा I निहित है<br>कथन में प्रारंभिक स्थापना लागत का उल्लेख ही नहीं है, और 'सभी' शब्द तो इस दावे को अत्यधिक व्यापक बना देता है, अतः अवधारणा II निहित नहीं है<br>इसलिए केवल अवधारणा I निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल अवधारणा I निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070600","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Four different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '6'.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की चार अलग-अलग स्थितियाँ दर्शाई गई हैं। उस संख्या का चयन कीजिए जो '6' वाले फलक के विपरीत फलक पर होगी।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first position 6 is seen with 4 and 5, in the third position 6 is seen with 2 and in the fourth position 6 is seen with 5 again<br>So 6 is adjacent to 4, 5 and 2 and cannot be opposite any of them<br>The faces of the dice here run from 2 to 7, so the only number left is 3, which therefore lies opposite 6<br>Hence the answer is 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"पहली स्थिति में 6 के साथ 4 तथा 5 दिखते हैं, तीसरी स्थिति में 6 के साथ 2 तथा चौथी स्थिति में फिर 5 दिखता है<br>अतः 6, फलक 4, 5 तथा 2 के सन्निकट है और इनमें से किसी के विपरीत नहीं हो सकता<br>इस पासे के फलक 2 से 7 तक हैं, अतः शेष बची एकमात्र संख्या 3 है, जो 6 के विपरीत है<br>इसलिए उत्तर 3 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070601","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), and (d), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c) तथा (d) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी निश्चित प्रकार से समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति अन्य चार से भिन्न है। शेष से भिन्न आकृति चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"e"},"2":{"en":"a"},"3":{"en":"b"},"4":{"en":"c"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each figure shows a small group of leaves joined at one point and in figures (a), (b), (d) and (e) the group carries three leaves placed in different turns<br>In figure (c) the group carries four leaves instead of three, so the number of leaves is different from the other figures<br>Hence figure (c) is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): c.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक आकृति में एक बिंदु पर जुड़ी पत्तियों का छोटा समूह है और आकृति (a), (b), (d) तथा (e) में समूह में तीन पत्तियाँ भिन्न घुमावों में हैं<br>आकृति (c) में तीन के स्थान पर चार पत्तियाँ हैं, अतः पत्तियों की संख्या अन्य आकृतियों से भिन्न है<br>इसलिए आकृति (c) अन्य से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): c है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070602","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), and (d), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c) तथा (d) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी निश्चित प्रकार से समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति अन्य चार से भिन्न है। शेष से भिन्न आकृति चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"b"},"2":{"en":"c"},"3":{"en":"d"},"4":{"en":"e"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In figures (a), (b), (d) and (e) a round shape has a piece cut away from it and the same cut-away piece is drawn separately below or beside it<br>In figure (c) the two parts are only shallow curved strips and there is no round body from which a piece could have been cut, so the make-up of the figure is different<br>Hence figure (c) is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): c.</b>","hi":"आकृति (a), (b), (d) तथा (e) में एक गोल आकार से एक भाग काटा गया है और वही कटा हुआ भाग अलग से नीचे या बगल में बनाया गया है<br>आकृति (c) में दोनों भाग केवल उथली वक्र पट्टियाँ हैं और ऐसा कोई गोल आकार नहीं है जिससे भाग काटा गया हो, अतः आकृति की रचना भिन्न है<br>इसलिए आकृति (c) अन्य से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): c है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070603","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks ( _ ) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br>r _ orrn _ r _ norrn _ r [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी में एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न बना रहे, इसके लिए निम्नलिखित चार विकल्पों में से किसी एक का प्रयोग करके रिक्त स्थान ( _ ) भरिए।<br>r _ orrn _ r _ norrn _ r [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ronr"},"2":{"en":"noro"},"3":{"en":"onro"},"4":{"en":"nnro"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Putting n, o, r and o in the four blanks gives r n o r r n o r r n o r r n o r<br>The block r n o r is repeated again and again from the very first letter<br>The other options break this repetition within the first few letters<br>So the correct set of letters is noro<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): noro.</b>","hi":"चारों रिक्त स्थानों में n, o, r तथा o भरने पर r n o r r n o r r n o r r n o r प्राप्त होता है<br>पहले अक्षर से ही r n o r खंड बार-बार दोहराया जाता है<br>अन्य विकल्प पहले कुछ अक्षरों में ही यह पुनरावृत्ति तोड़ देते हैं<br>अतः सही अक्षर-समूह noro है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): noro है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070604","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures (1,2,3,4) which will continue the same series as established by the five Problem Figures.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पाँच समस्या आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाने वाली आकृति उत्तर आकृतियों (1,2,3,4) में से चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In the problem figures the number of leaves keeps increasing in a fixed pattern and the whole leaf also turns step by step<br>Answer figure 2 carries the number of leaves and the turning position that come next in this pattern, while the other answer figures have the wrong number of leaves or the wrong turn<br>Hence answer figure 2 continues the series<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"समस्या आकृतियों में पत्तियों की संख्या एक निश्चित पैटर्न से बढ़ती जाती है और पूरी पत्ती भी चरण-दर-चरण घूमती है<br>उत्तर आकृति 2 में इसी पैटर्न के अनुसार अगली संख्या की पत्तियाँ तथा सही घूर्णन है, जबकि अन्य उत्तर आकृतियों में पत्तियों की संख्या या घूर्णन गलत है<br>अतः उत्तर आकृति 2 श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg"]}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070605","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which word does not share the same symmetrical spelling pattern as the others? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा शब्द अन्य शब्दों के समान सममित वर्तनी पैटर्न नहीं रखता? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"LEVEL"},"2":{"en":"RADAR"},"3":{"en":"CIVIC"},"4":{"en":"FRESH"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"LEVEL reads the same forwards and backwards, and the same is true of RADAR and CIVIC, so all three are palindromes<br>FRESH reversed becomes HSERF, which is not the same word, so it is not a palindrome<br>Hence FRESH does not share the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): FRESH.</b>","hi":"LEVEL आगे और पीछे दोनों ओर से एक ही पढ़ा जाता है, तथा RADAR और CIVIC भी वैसे ही हैं, अतः तीनों पैलिंड्रोम हैं<br>FRESH उल्टा करने पर HSERF बनता है, जो वही शब्द नहीं है, अतः यह पैलिंड्रोम नहीं है<br>इसलिए FRESH यह पैटर्न नहीं रखता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): FRESH है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070606","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which Indian Cabinet Minister was in the news for authoring the book \"Why Bharat Matters\"? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-से भारतीय कैबिनेट मंत्री पुस्तक \"व्हाय भारत मैटर्स\" के लेखन के कारण चर्चा में रहे? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajnath Singh","hi":"राजनाथ सिंह"},"2":{"en":"Amit Shah","hi":"अमित शाह"},"3":{"en":"Dr. S. Jaishankar","hi":"डॉ. एस. जयशंकर"},"4":{"en":"Nirmala Sitharaman","hi":"निर्मला सीतारमण"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Dr. S. Jaishankar</b><br><b>'Why Bharat Matters'</b> was authored by External Affairs Minister <b>Dr S. Jaishankar</b>, published in 2024, and it argues for an India-led approach to world affairs rooted in Indian civilisational thought.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• S. Jaishankar has also written <b>'The India Way: Strategies for an Uncertain World'</b> and <b>'Game Changer'</b>.<br>• He has served as <b>Foreign Secretary (2015-2018)</b> and India's Ambassador to China and the USA, and became External Affairs Minister in 2019.<br>• The book discusses <b>India's foreign policy choices, its role in a multipolar world and the idea of 'Bharat' as a civilisational state</b>.<br>• <b>Rajnath Singh</b>, <b>Amit Shah</b> and <b>Nirmala Sitharaman</b> are other senior ministers but did not author this book.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Dr S. Jaishankar authored 'Why Bharat Matters'.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – डॉ. एस. जयशंकर</b><br><b>'व्हाय भारत मैटर्स'</b> विदेश मंत्री <b>डॉ. एस. जयशंकर</b> द्वारा लिखी गई और 2024 में प्रकाशित हुई, जिसमें भारतीय सभ्यतागत चिंतन पर आधारित भारत-नेतृत्व वाले विश्व दृष्टिकोण का पक्ष रखा गया है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• एस. जयशंकर ने <b>'द इंडिया वे: स्ट्रैटेजीज फॉर एन अंसर्टन वर्ल्ड'</b> तथा <b>'गेम चेंजर'</b> भी लिखी हैं।<br>• वे <b>विदेश सचिव (2015-2018)</b> तथा चीन एवं अमेरिका में भारत के राजदूत रहे, और 2019 में विदेश मंत्री बने।<br>• यह पुस्तक <b>भारत की विदेश नीति के विकल्पों, बहुध्रुवीय विश्व में उसकी भूमिका तथा 'भारत' को सभ्यतागत राज्य के रूप में देखने</b> पर चर्चा करती है।<br>• <b>राजनाथ सिंह</b>, <b>अमित शाह</b> तथा <b>निर्मला सीतारमण</b> अन्य वरिष्ठ मंत्री हैं, परंतु इस पुस्तक के लेखक नहीं हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 'व्हाय भारत मैटर्स' के लेखक डॉ. एस. जयशंकर हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070607","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In cricket, what does the term “Duck” refer to? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"क्रिकेट में \"डक\" शब्द का क्या अर्थ है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A low bounce","hi":"कम उछाल"},"2":{"en":"A batsman scoring zero runs","hi":"बल्लेबाज द्वारा शून्य रन बनाना"},"3":{"en":"A wide delivery","hi":"वाइड गेंद"},"4":{"en":"A slow ball","hi":"धीमी गेंद"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – A batsman scoring zero runs</b><br>In cricket a <b>'duck'</b> means a batter is <b>dismissed without scoring any runs</b>; a 'golden duck' is a dismissal on the very first ball faced.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>'pair'</b> is two ducks in the two innings of a Test match, while a <b>'diamond duck'</b> is a dismissal without facing a ball, usually by run out.<br>• A wide is an illegal delivery outside the batter's reach, and a slow ball is a change of pace, both unrelated to the duck.<br>• The term is believed to come from '<b>duck's egg</b>', the shape of the zero on the scorecard.<br>• The highest individual score of 400 not out by Brian Lara and the most Test ducks record show the term's use at all levels.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because a duck means a batter scores zero runs.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बल्लेबाज द्वारा शून्य रन बनाना</b><br>क्रिकेट में <b>'डक'</b> का अर्थ है बल्लेबाज का <b>बिना कोई रन बनाए आउट</b> हो जाना; पहली ही गेंद पर आउट होना 'गोल्डन डक' कहलाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टेस्ट मैच की दोनों पारियों में शून्य पर आउट होना <b>'पेयर'</b> कहलाता है, तथा बिना गेंद खेले (सामान्यतः रन आउट) आउट होना <b>'डायमंड डक'</b>।<br>• वाइड बल्लेबाज की पहुँच से बाहर की अवैध गेंद है, और धीमी गेंद गति में परिवर्तन है, दोनों डक से असंबंधित हैं।<br>• माना जाता है कि यह शब्द '<b>डक्स एग</b>' (बत्तख का अंडा) से आया, जो स्कोरकार्ड पर शून्य का आकार दर्शाता है।<br>• ब्रायन लारा के 400 नाबाद तथा सर्वाधिक टेस्ट डक के रिकॉर्ड इस शब्द के सभी स्तरों पर प्रयोग को दर्शाते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि डक का अर्थ बल्लेबाज का शून्य रन बनाना है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070608","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Salient Features of the Constitution","question":{"en":"Which part of the Indian Constitution deals with the official language of the Union? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा भाग संघ की राजभाषा से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Part XII","hi":"भाग XII"},"2":{"en":"Part XV","hi":"भाग XV"},"3":{"en":"Part XVII","hi":"भाग XVII"},"4":{"en":"Part XIX","hi":"भाग XIX"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Part XVII</b><br><b>Part XVII of the Constitution (Articles 343 to 351)</b> deals with the <b>official language</b>, comprising the language of the Union, the regional languages and the language of the courts and legislation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 343</b> provides that Hindi in Devanagari script shall be the official language of the Union, and <b>Article 351</b> directs the Union to promote the spread of Hindi.<br>• Part XVII also provides for the <b>Official Languages Commission (Article 344)</b> and the Committee of Parliament on Official Language.<br>• <b>Part XII</b> deals with finance, property, contracts and suits, <b>Part XV</b> with elections and <b>Part XIX</b> with miscellaneous provisions such as protection of the President and Governors.<br>• The <b>Eighth Schedule</b>, which lists the recognised languages, is not part of Part XVII but is closely related to it.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Part XVII deals with the official language of the Union.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भाग XVII</b><br><b>संविधान का भाग XVII (अनुच्छेद 343 से 351)</b> <b>राजभाषा</b> से संबंधित है, जिसमें संघ की भाषा, प्रादेशिक भाषाएँ तथा न्यायालयों एवं विधान की भाषा सम्मिलित हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 343</b> प्रावधान करता है कि देवनागरी लिपि में हिंदी संघ की राजभाषा होगी, और <b>अनुच्छेद 351</b> हिंदी के प्रसार को निर्देशित करता है।<br>• भाग XVII में <b>राजभाषा आयोग (अनुच्छेद 344)</b> तथा राजभाषा पर संसदीय समिति का भी प्रावधान है।<br>• <b>भाग XII</b> वित्त, संपत्ति, संविदा तथा वादों से, <b>भाग XV</b> निर्वाचनों से तथा <b>भाग XIX</b> राष्ट्रपति एवं राज्यपालों के संरक्षण जैसे प्रकीर्ण प्रावधानों से संबंधित है।<br>• मान्यता प्राप्त भाषाओं की सूची वाली <b>आठवीं अनुसूची</b> भाग XVII का अंग नहीं है, परंतु उससे निकटता से जुड़ी है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि भाग XVII संघ की राजभाषा से संबंधित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070609","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Local Government","question":{"en":"Which was the first district in India to implement the third tier of Panchayati Raj governance? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत में पंचायती राज शासन के तृतीय स्तर को लागू करने वाला प्रथम जिला कौन-सा था? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bidar, Karnataka","hi":"बीदर, कर्नाटक"},"2":{"en":"Nagaur, Rajasthan","hi":"नागौर, राजस्थान"},"3":{"en":"Nadia, West Bengal","hi":"नदिया, पश्चिम बंगाल"},"4":{"en":"Palakkad, Kerala","hi":"पालक्काड, केरल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Nagaur, Rajasthan</b><br><b>Nagaur district in Rajasthan</b> was the first district in India to implement the <b>third tier of Panchayati Raj</b>, when Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru inaugurated the system at <b>Bagdari village on 2 October 1959</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Rajasthan was the first state to implement Panchayati Raj, following the recommendations of the <b>Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957)</b>.<br>• The three-tier structure consists of <b>Gram Panchayat at the village level, Panchayat Samiti at the block level and Zila Parishad at the district level</b>.<br>• The <b>73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992</b> gave constitutional status to panchayats by adding Part IX and the Eleventh Schedule with 29 subjects.<br>• <b>Andhra Pradesh</b> was the second state to implement the system, and <b>Bidar, Nadia and Palakkad</b> are not associated with the first implementation.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Nagaur was the first district to implement the third tier.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नागौर, राजस्थान</b><br><b>राजस्थान का नागौर जिला</b> भारत में <b>पंचायती राज के तृतीय स्तर</b> को लागू करने वाला प्रथम जिला था, जब प्रधानमंत्री जवाहरलाल नेहरू ने <b>2 अक्टूबर 1959</b> को <b>बागदरी गाँव</b> में इस प्रणाली का उद्घाटन किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>बलवंत राय मेहता समिति (1957)</b> की सिफारिशों के बाद राजस्थान पंचायती राज लागू करने वाला प्रथम राज्य था।<br>• त्रि-स्तरीय संरचना में <b>ग्राम स्तर पर ग्राम पंचायत, प्रखंड स्तर पर पंचायत समिति तथा जिला स्तर पर जिला परिषद</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• <b>73वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992</b> ने भाग IX तथा 29 विषयों वाली ग्यारहवीं अनुसूची जोड़कर पंचायतों को संवैधानिक दर्जा दिया।<br>• इस प्रणाली को लागू करने वाला दूसरा राज्य <b>आंध्र प्रदेश</b> था, तथा <b>बीदर, नदिया एवं पालक्काड</b> प्रथम क्रियान्वयन से संबंधित नहीं हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि नागौर तृतीय स्तर लागू करने वाला प्रथम जिला था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070610","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"The 'Lavani' folk music, known for its powerful rhythm and lyrics, originates from which state? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"'लावणी' लोक संगीत, जो अपनी प्रबल लय तथा बोल के लिए जाना जाता है, किस राज्य से उत्पन्न हुआ है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maharashtra","hi":"महाराष्ट्र"},"2":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"3":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"Karnataka","hi":"कर्नाटक"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Maharashtra</b><br><b>Lavani</b> is a popular folk song and dance form of <b>Maharashtra</b>, known for its <b>fast rhythm, powerful lyrics and expressive performance</b>, traditionally performed to the beats of the dholki.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Lavani is associated with the <b>tamasha</b> folk theatre tradition and is performed by both men and women, with the 'lavani' dancer wearing a nine-yard saree.<br>• It gained popularity in the <b>18th-19th centuries</b>, especially under the Maratha rulers and the Peshwas.<br>• The main instruments used are the <b>dholki, tasha, manjira and dimdi</b>, and Lavani songs often deal with social themes and love.<br>• Other Maharashtra folk forms are <b>Tamasha, Koli, Povada and Dhangari Gaja</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Lavani originates from Maharashtra.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – महाराष्ट्र</b><br><b>लावणी</b> <b>महाराष्ट्र</b> का लोकप्रिय लोकगीत एवं नृत्य रूप है, जो <b>तेज लय, प्रबल बोल तथा भावपूर्ण प्रस्तुति</b> के लिए जाना जाता है और परंपरागत रूप से ढोलकी की ताल पर प्रस्तुत किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लावणी <b>तमाशा</b> लोक रंगमंच परंपरा से जुड़ी है और इसे पुरुष तथा महिला दोनों प्रस्तुत करते हैं, जिसमें 'लावणी' नर्तकी नौ गज की साड़ी पहनती है।<br>• यह <b>18वीं-19वीं शताब्दी</b> में, विशेषतः मराठा शासकों तथा पेशवाओं के समय लोकप्रिय हुई।<br>• इसके मुख्य वाद्य <b>ढोलकी, ताशा, मंजीरा तथा डिम्डी</b> हैं, और लावणी के बोल प्रायः सामाजिक विषयों तथा प्रेम पर आधारित होते हैं।<br>• महाराष्ट्र के अन्य लोक रूप <b>तमाशा, कोली, पोवाड़ा तथा ढंगरी गजा</b> हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि लावणी महाराष्ट्र से उत्पन्न हुई है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070611","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"<b>Statement I:</b> BRICS established a Contingent Reserve Arrangement (CRA) to tackle short-term balance of payments pressures.<br><b>Statement II:</b> The 11th BRICS Parliamentary Forum was held in Brasilia, Brazil on 4–5 June 2025.<br>Which statements is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>कथन I:</b> ब्रिक्स ने अल्पकालिक भुगतान संतुलन दबावों से निपटने हेतु आकस्मिक आरक्षित व्यवस्था (CRA) स्थापित की।<br><b>कथन II:</b> 11वाँ ब्रिक्स संसदीय फोरम 4–5 जून 2025 को ब्रासीलिया, ब्राज़ील में आयोजित हुआ।<br>कौन-से कथन <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both I and II are correct","hi":"I तथा II दोनों सही हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I is correct","hi":"केवल I सही है"},"3":{"en":"Only II is correct","hi":"केवल II सही है"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are incorrect","hi":"I तथा II दोनों गलत हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Both I and II are correct</b><br>Both statements are correct – <b>BRICS</b> set up the <b>Contingent Reserve Arrangement (CRA)</b> in 2014 to provide short-term balance of payments support to members, and the <b>11th BRICS Parliamentary Forum</b> was held at <b>Brasília, Brazil</b> in <b>June 2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The CRA was established along with the <b>New Development Bank</b> at the Fortaleza Summit in 2014, with an initial size of <b>USD 100 billion</b>.<br>• The CRA is a <b>self-managed liquidity mechanism</b> that works like a network of swap lines, and India's contribution is USD 18 billion.<br>• The 11th BRICS Parliamentary Forum was attended by presiding officers of the members' legislatures and focused on <b>multilateralism, sustainable development and the role of parliaments</b>.<br>• Brazil held the BRICS chairship in 2025, with the summit theme of cooperation for a fair and sustainable world.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because both statements about the CRA and the Parliamentary Forum are correct.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – I तथा II दोनों सही हैं</b><br>दोनों कथन सही हैं – <b>ब्रिक्स</b> ने 2014 में सदस्यों को अल्पकालिक भुगतान संतुलन सहायता देने हेतु <b>आकस्मिक आरक्षित व्यवस्था (CRA)</b> स्थापित की, तथा <b>11वाँ ब्रिक्स संसदीय फोरम</b> <b>जून 2025</b> में <b>ब्रासीलिया, ब्राज़ील</b> में आयोजित हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CRA 2014 के फोर्टालेजा शिखर सम्मेलन में <b>न्यू डेवलपमेंट बैंक</b> के साथ स्थापित हुई, जिसका प्रारंभिक आकार <b>100 अरब USD</b> था।<br>• CRA एक <b>स्व-प्रबंधित तरलता व्यवस्था</b> है जो स्वैप लाइनों के नेटवर्क की तरह कार्य करती है, और भारत का अंशदान 18 अरब USD है।<br>• 11वें ब्रिक्स संसदीय फोरम में सदस्य देशों के विधानमंडलों के पीठासीन अधिकारियों ने भाग लिया और इसका केंद्र <b>बहुपक्षवाद, सतत विकास तथा संसदों की भूमिका</b> रहा।<br>• 2025 में ब्रिक्स की अध्यक्षता ब्राज़ील के पास थी, जिसकी शिखर बैठक का विषय न्यायपूर्ण एवं सतत विश्व हेतु सहयोग था।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि CRA तथा संसदीय फोरम से संबंधित दोनों कथन सही हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070612","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"Mughal architecture is most prominently known for which element? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मुगल वास्तुकला अपने किस तत्व के लिए सर्वाधिक प्रसिद्ध है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Stupas","hi":"स्तूप"},"2":{"en":"Domes and minarets","hi":"गुंबद तथा मीनारें"},"3":{"en":"Step wells","hi":"बावड़ियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Wooden structures","hi":"लकड़ी की संरचनाएँ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Domes and minarets</b><br>Mughal architecture is most prominently known for its <b>domes and minarets</b>, seen in the <b>Taj Mahal, Humayun's Tomb, Jama Masjid and Fatehpur Sikri</b>, along with arches, pietra dura inlay and symmetrical gardens.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Mughals developed the <b>double dome, the bulbous onion dome, the iwan and the charbagh garden</b> layout.<br>• <b>Humayun's Tomb</b> (1565) is regarded as the first mature Mughal building and a prototype of the Taj Mahal.<br>• The <b>Red Fort, Jama Masjid and Taj Mahal</b> were built by Shah Jahan, whose reign is called the golden age of Mughal architecture.<br>• <b>Stupas</b> belong to Buddhist architecture, <b>step wells</b> mainly to western India and wooden structures to Himalayan and south Indian temple traditions.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Mughal architecture is best known for domes and minarets.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – गुंबद तथा मीनारें</b><br>मुगल वास्तुकला <b>गुंबद तथा मीनारों</b> के लिए सर्वाधिक प्रसिद्ध है, जो <b>ताजमहल, हुमायूँ का मकबरा, जामा मस्जिद तथा फतेहपुर सीकरी</b> में दिखती हैं, साथ ही मेहराब, पिएत्रा दूरा जड़ाऊ कार्य तथा सममित उद्यान।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मुगलों ने <b>दोहरा गुंबद, प्याज़ी गुंबद, ईवान तथा चारबाग उद्यान</b> का विन्यास विकसित किया।<br>• <b>हुमायूँ का मकबरा</b> (1565) प्रथम परिपक्व मुगल इमारत तथा ताजमहल का पूर्वरूप माना जाता है।<br>• <b>लाल किला, जामा मस्जिद तथा ताजमहल</b> शाहजहाँ ने बनवाए, जिनका काल मुगल वास्तुकला का स्वर्णयुग कहलाता है।<br>• <b>स्तूप</b> बौद्ध वास्तुकला के, <b>बावड़ियाँ</b> मुख्यतः पश्चिमी भारत के तथा लकड़ी की संरचनाएँ हिमालयी एवं दक्षिण भारतीय मंदिर परंपरा की हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि मुगल वास्तुकला गुंबदों तथा मीनारों के लिए सर्वाधिक जानी जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070613","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements:<br>1. Leander Paes has won an Olympic medal in tennis.<br>2. P.V. Sindhu is the only Indian woman with two Olympic medals in badminton.<br>3. Abhinav Bindra has two Olympic medals.<br>Which of the following statements is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार करें:<br>1. लिएंडर पेस ने टेनिस में ओलंपिक पदक जीता है।<br>2. पी. वी. सिंधु बैडमिंटन में दो ओलंपिक पदक जीतने वाली एकमात्र भारतीय महिला हैं।<br>3. अभिनव बिंद्रा के दो ओलंपिक पदक हैं।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से कथन <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1 and 2 are correct","hi":"केवल 1 तथा 2 सही हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only 2 and 3 are correct","hi":"केवल 2 तथा 3 सही हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only 1 and 3 are correct","hi":"केवल 1 तथा 3 सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"1,2 and 3 are correct","hi":"1, 2 तथा 3 सभी सही हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Only 1 and 2 are correct</b><br>Statements 1 and 2 are correct – <b>Leander Paes</b> won a <b>bronze medal in tennis</b> at the Atlanta Olympics 1996, and <b>P.V. Sindhu</b> is the only Indian woman with <b>two Olympic badminton medals</b> (silver 2016, bronze 2020); statement 3 is wrong because <b>Abhinav Bindra</b> has only <b>one</b> Olympic medal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Leander Paes's bronze was India's first individual Olympic medal since 1952, and he is also an Olympic tennis record holder for appearances.<br>• Sindhu won silver at <b>Rio 2016</b> and bronze at <b>Tokyo 2020</b>, becoming the first Indian woman to win two individual Olympic medals.<br>• <b>Abhinav Bindra</b> won gold in the 10 m air rifle at <b>Beijing 2008</b> and finished fourth in 2016; he did not win a second medal.<br>• Other Indian Olympic medallists include <b>Neeraj Chopra (gold 2020, silver 2024), Sushil Kumar and Manu Bhaker</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because only statements 1 and 2 are correct.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1 तथा 2 सही हैं</b><br>कथन 1 तथा 2 सही हैं – <b>लिएंडर पेस</b> ने 1996 के अटलांटा ओलंपिक में <b>टेनिस में कांस्य पदक</b> जीता, और <b>पी. वी. सिंधु</b> <b>दो ओलंपिक बैडमिंटन पदक</b> (रजत 2016, कांस्य 2020) जीतने वाली एकमात्र भारतीय महिला हैं; कथन 3 गलत है क्योंकि <b>अभिनव बिंद्रा</b> के पास केवल <b>एक</b> ओलंपिक पदक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लिएंडर पेस का कांस्य 1952 के बाद भारत का प्रथम व्यक्तिगत ओलंपिक पदक था, और वे ओलंपिक में सर्वाधिक बार भाग लेने के टेनिस रिकॉर्डधारी भी हैं।<br>• सिंधु ने <b>रियो 2016</b> में रजत तथा <b>टोक्यो 2020</b> में कांस्य जीता और दो व्यक्तिगत ओलंपिक पदक जीतने वाली प्रथम भारतीय महिला बनीं।<br>• <b>अभिनव बिंद्रा</b> ने <b>बीजिंग 2008</b> में 10 मीटर एयर राइफल में स्वर्ण जीता और 2016 में चौथे स्थान पर रहे; दूसरा पदक नहीं मिला।<br>• अन्य भारतीय ओलंपिक पदक विजेताओं में <b>नीरज चोपड़ा (स्वर्ण 2020, रजत 2024), सुशील कुमार तथा मनु भाकर</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि केवल कथन 1 तथा 2 सही हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070614","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The 'Mission Karmayogi' launched by the Government of India is aimed at: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत सरकार द्वारा शुरू किया गया 'मिशन कर्मयोगी' किस उद्देश्य से है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Skill development for youth","hi":"युवाओं के कौशल विकास हेतु"},"2":{"en":"Reforming the recruitment of IAS officers","hi":"IAS अधिकारियों की भर्ती में सुधार हेतु"},"3":{"en":"Capacity building of civil servants","hi":"सिविल सेवकों की क्षमता निर्माण हेतु"},"4":{"en":"Digital literacy for rural India","hi":"ग्रामीण भारत हेतु डिजिटल साक्षरता हेतु"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Capacity building of civil servants</b><br><b>Mission Karmayogi</b>, launched in <b>2020</b>, is the <b>National Programme for Civil Services Capacity Building (NPCSCB)</b>, aimed at developing the <b>competencies, attitudes and skills of civil servants</b> to make them more citizen-centric and future-ready.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Its institutional architecture includes the <b>Prime Minister's Public Human Resources Council, the Capacity Building Commission and the Special Purpose Vehicle 'Karmayogi Bharat'</b>.<br>• The <b>iGOT Karmayogi</b> platform provides online training courses for government employees at all levels.<br>• The programme shifts from rule-based to <b>role-based training</b> and emphasises lifelong learning and performance.<br>• Skill development for youth is handled by the Skill India Mission and PMKVY, and rural digital literacy by the PMGDISHA scheme.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Mission Karmayogi is aimed at capacity building of civil servants.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सिविल सेवकों की क्षमता निर्माण हेतु</b><br><b>मिशन कर्मयोगी</b>, जो <b>2020</b> में शुरू हुआ, <b>सिविल सेवा क्षमता निर्माण हेतु राष्ट्रीय कार्यक्रम (NPCSCB)</b> है, जिसका उद्देश्य <b>सिविल सेवकों की योग्यता, दृष्टिकोण तथा कौशल</b> विकसित कर उन्हें अधिक नागरिक-केंद्रित एवं भविष्य के लिए तैयार बनाना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी संस्थागत संरचना में <b>प्रधानमंत्री लोक मानव संसाधन परिषद, क्षमता निर्माण आयोग तथा विशेष प्रयोजन वाहन 'कर्मयोगी भारत'</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• <b>iGOT कर्मयोगी</b> प्लेटफॉर्म सभी स्तरों के सरकारी कर्मचारियों को ऑनलाइन प्रशिक्षण पाठ्यक्रम उपलब्ध कराता है।<br>• यह कार्यक्रम नियम-आधारित से <b>भूमिका-आधारित प्रशिक्षण</b> की ओर बदलाव करता है और आजीवन अधिगम तथा प्रदर्शन पर बल देता है।<br>• युवाओं के कौशल विकास का कार्य स्किल इंडिया मिशन तथा PMKVY करते हैं, और ग्रामीण डिजिटल साक्षरता का कार्य PMGDISHA योजना।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि मिशन कर्मयोगी सिविल सेवकों की क्षमता निर्माण हेतु है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070615","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: State News","question":{"en":"Which Indian state hosted the Global Investors Summit 2025 in February? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"फरवरी में ग्लोबल इन्वेस्टर्स समिट 2025 की मेजबानी किस भारतीय राज्य ने की? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"2":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"Maharashtra","hi":"महाराष्ट्र"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Madhya Pradesh</b><br>The <b>Global Investors Summit 2025</b> was hosted by <b>Madhya Pradesh</b> in <b>February 2025</b> at Bhopal, under the banner 'Invest MP', and it attracted investment proposals and MoUs across sectors such as manufacturing, renewable energy and IT.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The summit was preceded by <b>regional industry conclaves</b> in different divisions of the state and focused on making Madhya Pradesh an industrial hub.<br>• Madhya Pradesh has emphasised sectors such as <b>textiles, food processing, pharmaceuticals, automobiles and tourism</b> for investment.<br>• Gujarat holds its own <b>Vibrant Gujarat Global Summit</b>, and Uttar Pradesh held its Global Investors Summit in 2023.<br>• State investment summits are a key instrument of <b>competitive federalism</b> and of attracting FDI and domestic investment.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Madhya Pradesh hosted the Global Investors Summit 2025 in February.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मध्य प्रदेश</b><br><b>ग्लोबल इन्वेस्टर्स समिट 2025</b> की मेजबानी <b>मध्य प्रदेश</b> ने <b>फरवरी 2025</b> में भोपाल में 'इन्वेस्ट एमपी' के नाम से की, जिसमें विनिर्माण, अक्षय ऊर्जा तथा आईटी जैसे क्षेत्रों में निवेश प्रस्ताव एवं समझौता ज्ञापन प्राप्त हुए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• समिट से पहले राज्य के विभिन्न संभागों में <b>क्षेत्रीय उद्योग सम्मेलन</b> हुए और इसका उद्देश्य मध्य प्रदेश को औद्योगिक केंद्र बनाना था।<br>• मध्य प्रदेश ने निवेश हेतु <b>वस्त्र, खाद्य प्रसंस्करण, औषधि, ऑटोमोबाइल तथा पर्यटन</b> जैसे क्षेत्रों पर बल दिया।<br>• गुजरात अपना <b>वाइब्रेंट गुजरात ग्लोबल समिट</b> आयोजित करता है, और उत्तर प्रदेश ने 2023 में अपना ग्लोबल इन्वेस्टर्स समिट किया।<br>• राज्यों के निवेश सम्मेलन <b>प्रतिस्पर्धी संघवाद</b> तथा प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी एवं घरेलू निवेश आकर्षित करने का प्रमुख साधन हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि फरवरी में ग्लोबल इन्वेस्टर्स समिट 2025 की मेजबानी मध्य प्रदेश ने की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070616","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To regulate the conduct of civil trials","hi":"सिविल विचारणों के संचालन का नियमन करना"},"2":{"en":"To consolidate and amend the law relating to evidence","hi":"साक्ष्य से संबंधित विधि का समेकन तथा संशोधन करना"},"3":{"en":"To reform criminal sentencing procedures","hi":"आपराधिक दंड प्रक्रिया में सुधार करना"},"4":{"en":"To establish fast-track courts","hi":"फास्ट-ट्रैक न्यायालयों की स्थापना करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To consolidate and amend the law relating to evidence</b><br>The <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b> is described in its preamble as an Act <b>to consolidate and to provide for the general rules and procedures of evidence</b>, replacing the Indian Evidence Act, 1872.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The BSA <b>replaced the Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>, along with the BNS and BNSS.<br>• Its key changes include recognition of <b>electronic and digital records as primary evidence</b>, rules for electronic evidence certification and the admissibility of <b>oral and documentary evidence in digital form</b>.<br>• The Act applies to <b>all judicial proceedings in or before a court</b>, both civil and criminal, so option (1) is too narrow.<br>• Sentencing reform is dealt with in the BNS and fast-track courts are established under the BNSS and special statutes.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the BSA consolidates and amends the law of evidence.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – साक्ष्य से संबंधित विधि का समेकन तथा संशोधन करना</b><br><b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023</b> की प्रस्तावना में इसे <b>साक्ष्य के सामान्य नियमों तथा प्रक्रियाओं का समेकन एवं प्रावधान</b> करने वाला अधिनियम कहा गया है, जो भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872 का स्थान लेता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BSA ने <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872 का स्थान लिया</b> और BNS तथा BNSS के साथ <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुआ।<br>• इसके प्रमुख परिवर्तनों में <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक एवं डिजिटल अभिलेखों को प्राथमिक साक्ष्य</b> के रूप में मान्यता, इलेक्ट्रॉनिक साक्ष्य प्रमाणन के नियम तथा <b>डिजिटल रूप में मौखिक एवं दस्तावेजी साक्ष्य</b> की ग्राह्यता सम्मिलित है।<br>• यह अधिनियम <b>न्यायालय में या उसके समक्ष सभी न्यायिक कार्यवाहियों</b>, सिविल तथा आपराधिक दोनों पर लागू होता है, इसलिए विकल्प (1) संकीर्ण है।<br>• दंड-प्रक्रिया में सुधार BNS में है तथा फास्ट-ट्रैक न्यायालय BNSS एवं विशेष अधिनियमों के अंतर्गत स्थापित होते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि BSA साक्ष्य विधि का समेकन एवं संशोधन करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070617","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Which layer of the Earth is primarily responsible for generating its magnetic field? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पृथ्वी की कौन-सी परत मुख्य रूप से उसका चुंबकीय क्षेत्र उत्पन्न करने के लिए उत्तरदायी है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Crust","hi":"भूपर्पटी"},"2":{"en":"Mantle","hi":"मैंटल"},"3":{"en":"Outer Core","hi":"बाहरी क्रोड"},"4":{"en":"Inner Core","hi":"आंतरिक क्रोड"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Outer Core</b><br>The <b>outer core</b>, a layer of <b>liquid iron and nickel</b>, generates the earth's magnetic field through the <b>geodynamo effect</b>, as its convecting, rotating conducting fluid produces electric currents.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The outer core lies between about <b>2,900 km and 5,150 km</b> depth and is liquid, as shown by the absence of S-waves.<br>• The <b>inner core is solid</b> because of enormous pressure, and the <b>mantle</b> is solid but slowly flowing rock.<br>• Earth's magnetic field has <b>reversed polarity many times</b>, recorded in the striped magnetic anomalies of the ocean floor.<br>• The magnetic field protects the earth from the <b>solar wind</b> and produces auroras at the poles.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the outer core is responsible for the earth's magnetic field.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – बाहरी क्रोड</b><br><b>बाहरी क्रोड</b>, जो <b>तरल लोहा तथा निकल</b> की परत है, <b>भू-डायनेमो प्रभाव</b> से पृथ्वी का चुंबकीय क्षेत्र उत्पन्न करता है, क्योंकि उसका संवहनशील एवं घूर्णनशील चालक तरल विद्युत धाराएँ पैदा करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बाहरी क्रोड लगभग <b>2,900 किमी से 5,150 किमी</b> गहराई के बीच है और तरल है, जैसा S-तरंगों की अनुपस्थिति से स्पष्ट होता है।<br>• अत्यधिक दाब के कारण <b>आंतरिक क्रोड ठोस</b> है, तथा <b>मैंटल</b> ठोस परंतु धीमी गति से बहने वाली चट्टान है।<br>• पृथ्वी के चुंबकीय क्षेत्र की <b>ध्रुवीयता कई बार उलटी</b> हुई है, जो महासागरीय तल की पट्टीदार चुंबकीय विषमताओं में अंकित है।<br>• चुंबकीय क्षेत्र पृथ्वी को <b>सौर पवन</b> से बचाता है और ध्रुवों पर ध्रुवीय ज्योति उत्पन्न करता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि पृथ्वी का चुंबकीय क्षेत्र बाहरी क्रोड के कारण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070618","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"What is the full form of ISRO’s “NAVIC” system? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ISRO की \"NavIC\" प्रणाली का पूर्ण रूप क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Navigation India for Communication","hi":"नेविगेशन इंडिया फॉर कम्युनिकेशन (Navigation India for Communication)"},"2":{"en":"Navigation with Indian Constellation","hi":"नेविगेशन विद इंडियन कॉन्स्टलेशन (Navigation with Indian Constellation)"},"3":{"en":"National Indian Vehicular Information Control","hi":"नेशनल इंडियन व्हीक्युलर इन्फॉर्मेशन कंट्रोल (National Indian Vehicular Information Control)"},"4":{"en":"Navigational Indian Vehicle Intelligence Center","hi":"नेविगेशनल इंडियन व्हीकल इंटेलिजेंस सेंटर (Navigational Indian Vehicle Intelligence Center)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Navigation with Indian Constellation</b><br><b>NavIC</b> stands for <b>'Navigation with Indian Constellation'</b>, India's regional satellite navigation system built by ISRO, earlier known as <b>IRNSS (Indian Regional Navigation Satellite System)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NavIC provides accurate <b>position, navigation and timing</b> services over India and about 1,500 km around it, with an extended service area.<br>• It consists of satellites in <b>geostationary and geosynchronous orbits</b> and offers a Standard Positioning Service and a Restricted Service.<br>• NavIC is used in <b>vehicle tracking, disaster management, fishing, surveying, timing and emergency warning systems</b>.<br>• Its applications include the <b>'Khanan' and 'Poshan' apps</b> and devices certified by the Indian government.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because NavIC stands for Navigation with Indian Constellation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नेविगेशन विद इंडियन कॉन्स्टलेशन (Navigation with Indian Constellation)</b><br><b>NavIC</b> का पूर्ण रूप <b>'नेविगेशन विद इंडियन कॉन्स्टलेशन'</b> है, जो ISRO द्वारा निर्मित भारत की क्षेत्रीय उपग्रह नौवहन प्रणाली है और पहले <b>IRNSS (भारतीय क्षेत्रीय नौवहन उपग्रह प्रणाली)</b> कहलाती थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NavIC भारत तथा उसके लगभग 1,500 किमी के आसपास के क्षेत्र में सटीक <b>स्थिति, नौवहन तथा समय</b> सेवाएँ देता है, साथ ही विस्तारित सेवा क्षेत्र भी।<br>• इसमें <b>भू-स्थैतिक एवं भू-तुल्यकालिक कक्षाओं</b> के उपग्रह हैं और यह मानक स्थिति सेवा तथा प्रतिबंधित सेवा प्रदान करता है।<br>• NavIC का उपयोग <b>वाहन ट्रैकिंग, आपदा प्रबंधन, मत्स्यन, सर्वेक्षण, समय-निर्धारण तथा आपातकालीन चेतावनी प्रणालियों</b> में होता है।<br>• इसके अनुप्रयोगों में <b>'खनन' तथा 'पोषण' ऐप</b> तथा भारत सरकार द्वारा प्रमाणित उपकरण सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि NavIC का अर्थ Navigation with Indian Constellation है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070619","section":"GK","topic":"Chemistry: Periodic Table","question":{"en":"Which element has the highest electronegativity? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस तत्व की विद्युतऋणता सर्वाधिक है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Oxygen","hi":"ऑक्सीजन"},"2":{"en":"Nitrogen","hi":"नाइट्रोजन"},"3":{"en":"Fluorine","hi":"फ्लोरीन"},"4":{"en":"Chlorine","hi":"क्लोरीन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Fluorine</b><br><b>Fluorine</b> has the highest <b>electronegativity</b> of all elements (3.98 on the Pauling scale), because of its small atomic size and the need for only one electron to complete its octet.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Electronegativity <b>increases across a period</b> and <b>decreases down a group</b>; hence fluorine exceeds chlorine, bromine and iodine.<br>• The order among the halogens is <b>F > Cl > Br > I</b>, and among the elements in option, F (3.98) > O (3.44) > N (3.04) > Cl (3.16).<br>• Fluorine is the most reactive non-metal and the most powerful oxidising agent, reacting with almost all elements.<br>• Electronegativity is a relative concept, measured by the <b>Pauling, Mulliken and Allred-Rochow</b> scales, and noble gases are excluded from the comparison.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because fluorine has the highest electronegativity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – फ्लोरीन</b><br>सभी तत्वों में <b>फ्लोरीन</b> की <b>विद्युतऋणता</b> सर्वाधिक है (पॉलिंग पैमाने पर 3.98), क्योंकि इसका परमाणु आकार छोटा है और अष्टक पूरा करने के लिए उसे केवल एक इलेक्ट्रॉन चाहिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विद्युतऋणता <b>आवर्त में बढ़ती</b> तथा <b>समूह में नीचे घटती</b> है; इसलिए फ्लोरीन क्लोरीन, ब्रोमीन तथा आयोडीन से अधिक विद्युतऋणी है।<br>• हैलोजन में क्रम <b>F > Cl > Br > I</b> है, तथा विकल्पों के तत्वों में F (3.98) > O (3.44) > Cl (3.16) > N (3.04)।<br>• फ्लोरीन सर्वाधिक क्रियाशील अधातु तथा सर्वाधिक प्रबल ऑक्सीकारक है, जो लगभग सभी तत्वों से अभिक्रिया करती है।<br>• विद्युतऋणता एक सापेक्ष अवधारणा है, जिसे <b>पॉलिंग, मुल्लिकेन तथा एल्रेड-रोशो</b> पैमानों से मापा जाता है, और उत्कृष्ट गैसों को तुलना से बाहर रखा जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि फ्लोरीन की विद्युतऋणता सर्वाधिक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070620","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which of the following describes Indian classical music where the vocalist and instrumentalist converse most of the time? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय शास्त्रीय संगीत का कौन-सा रूप वर्णित है जिसमें गायक तथा वादक अधिकांश समय संवाद करते हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dhrupad","hi":"ध्रुपद"},"2":{"en":"Bhajan","hi":"भजन"},"3":{"en":"Tarana","hi":"तराना"},"4":{"en":"Khayal","hi":"खयाल"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Khayal</b><br><b>Khayal</b> is the most prominent form of present-day <b>Hindustani vocal music</b> and allows the most <b>freedom of improvisation</b>, so that the vocalist and the accompanying instrumentalist can engage in a musical dialogue through alap, taan and sawal-jawab passages.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Khayal has two parts – the <b>sthayi (astayi)</b> in the lower register and the <b>antara</b> in the upper register – and is sung in a raga with a tala.<br>• The <b>sawal-jawab</b> (question-answer) exchange between vocalist and sarangi or tabla player is a hallmark of khayal performance.<br>• <b>Dhrupad</b> is an older, more austere form with a fixed structure, <b>tarana</b> uses meaningless syllables and bhajan is devotional song, not art music.<br>• Great khayal exponents include <b>Amir Khusrau's successors, Faiyaz Khan, Bhimsen Joshi, Kishori Amonkar and Kumar Gandharva</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because khayal allows the conversational improvisation described.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – खयाल</b><br><b>खयाल</b> आज के <b>हिंदुस्तानी स्वर संगीत</b> का सर्वाधिक प्रचलित रूप है और इसमें <b>आलाप, तान तथा सवाल-जवाब</b> के माध्यम से सबसे अधिक सृजनात्मक स्वतंत्रता मिलती है, जिससे गायक तथा साथी वादक के बीच संगीतमय संवाद बनता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• खयाल के दो भाग होते हैं – निचले सप्तक में <b>स्थायी</b> तथा ऊँचे सप्तक में <b>अंतरा</b> – और इसे राग तथा ताल में गाया जाता है।<br>• गायक तथा सारंगी या तबला वादक के बीच <b>सवाल-जवाब</b> का आदान-प्रदान खयाल प्रस्तुति की विशेषता है।<br>• <b>ध्रुपद</b> अधिक प्राचीन एवं गंभीर रूप है जिसकी संरचना निश्चित होती है, <b>तराना</b> में अर्थहीन अक्षर प्रयुक्त होते हैं तथा भजन भक्ति गीत है, शास्त्रीय संगीत नहीं।<br>• प्रसिद्ध खयाल गायकों में <b>फैयाज खाँ, भीमसेन जोशी, किशोरी अमोनकर तथा कुमार गंधर्व</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि वर्णित संवादात्मक सृजनात्मकता खयाल में मिलती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070621","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Which layer of the Earth is the densest? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पृथ्वी की कौन-सी परत सर्वाधिक घनत्व वाली है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Crust","hi":"भूपर्पटी"},"2":{"en":"Mantle","hi":"मैंटल"},"3":{"en":"Outer Core","hi":"बाहरी क्रोड"},"4":{"en":"Inner Core","hi":"आंतरिक क्रोड"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Inner Core</b><br>The <b>inner core</b> is the <b>densest layer of the earth</b>, made of <b>solid iron and nickel</b> with a density of about <b>13 g/cm³</b>, because of the enormous pressure at the centre.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Densities increase with depth – the <b>crust is about 2.7-3 g/cm³, the mantle 3.3-5.5 g/cm³, the outer core 9.9-12.2 g/cm³ and the inner core about 12.8-13.1 g/cm³</b>.<br>• The inner core is solid despite the high temperature because the <b>pressure keeps the iron in a solid state</b>.<br>• The boundary between the outer and inner core is the <b>Lehmann discontinuity</b>.<br>• The earth's average density is about 5.5 g/cm³, much higher than surface rocks, which proved the existence of a dense core.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the inner core has the highest density.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – आंतरिक क्रोड</b><br><b>आंतरिक क्रोड</b> <b>पृथ्वी की सर्वाधिक घनत्व वाली परत</b> है, जो <b>ठोस लोहा तथा निकल</b> से बनी है और जिसका घनत्व लगभग <b>13 ग्राम/घन सेमी</b> है, क्योंकि केंद्र पर अत्यधिक दाब है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गहराई के साथ घनत्व बढ़ता है – <b>भूपर्पटी लगभग 2.7-3, मैंटल 3.3-5.5, बाहरी क्रोड 9.9-12.2 तथा आंतरिक क्रोड लगभग 12.8-13.1 ग्राम/घन सेमी</b>।<br>• अधिक तापमान के बावजूद आंतरिक क्रोड ठोस है, क्योंकि <b>दाब लोहे को ठोस अवस्था में बनाए रखता है</b>।<br>• बाहरी तथा आंतरिक क्रोड के बीच की सीमा <b>लेहमान असंबद्धता</b> है।<br>• पृथ्वी का औसत घनत्व लगभग 5.5 ग्राम/घन सेमी है, जो सतही चट्टानों से बहुत अधिक है और यह घने क्रोड की उपस्थिति सिद्ध करता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि आंतरिक क्रोड का घनत्व सर्वाधिक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070622","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Vijayanagara and Bahmani Kingdom","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements regarding the Bahmani Kingdom is INCORRECT? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बहमनी साम्राज्य के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन <b>गलत</b> है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was founded by Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah.","hi":"इसकी स्थापना अलाउद्दीन हसन बहमन शाह ने की।"},"2":{"en":"It was constantly in conflict with the Vijayanagara Empire.","hi":"यह विजयनगर साम्राज्य के साथ लगातार संघर्ष में रहा।"},"3":{"en":"Mahmud Gawan was a powerful minister and reformer in the kingdom.","hi":"महमूद गवाँ इस साम्राज्य का शक्तिशाली मंत्री तथा सुधारक था।"},"4":{"en":"It was known for its extensive sea trade with European powers.","hi":"यह यूरोपीय शक्तियों के साथ व्यापक समुद्री व्यापार के लिए जाना जाता था।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – It was known for its extensive sea trade with European powers.</b><br>The <b>incorrect</b> statement is option (4), because the Bahmani Kingdom's overseas trade was carried on mainly by <b>Arab, Persian and Indian merchants</b> with West Asia; extensive direct sea trade with <b>European powers</b> developed only later, after the Portuguese arrived in 1498.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Bahmani Kingdom was founded in <b>1347 by Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah</b> with its capital at Gulbarga, later shifting to Bidar.<br>• Its four-century-long rivalry with <b>Vijayanagara</b> over the Raichur doab, Tungabhadra region and the Krishna-Godavari delta is well documented.<br>• <b>Mahmud Gawan</b>, the prime minister under Muhammad Shah III, reformed the administration, divided the kingdom into eight tarafs and founded the Madrasa at Bidar.<br>• The kingdom declined after Gawan's execution in 1481 and broke up into the <b>five Deccan Sultanates – Bijapur, Golconda, Ahmadnagar, Bidar and Berar</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the statement about extensive sea trade with European powers is incorrect.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – यह यूरोपीय शक्तियों के साथ व्यापक समुद्री व्यापार के लिए जाना जाता था।</b><br><b>गलत</b> कथन विकल्प (4) है, क्योंकि बहमनी साम्राज्य का विदेशी व्यापार मुख्यतः <b>अरब, फारसी तथा भारतीय व्यापारियों</b> द्वारा पश्चिम एशिया से होता था; <b>यूरोपीय शक्तियों</b> के साथ व्यापक प्रत्यक्ष समुद्री व्यापार 1498 में पुर्तगालियों के आगमन के बाद ही विकसित हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बहमनी साम्राज्य की स्थापना <b>1347 में अलाउद्दीन हसन बहमन शाह</b> ने गुलबर्गा को राजधानी बनाकर की, जो बाद में बीदर स्थानांतरित हुई।<br>• रायचूर दोआब, तुंगभद्रा क्षेत्र तथा कृष्णा-गोदावरी डेल्टा पर <b>विजयनगर</b> के साथ इसका चार शताब्दी लंबा संघर्ष प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• मुहम्मद शाह तृतीय के अंतर्गत प्रधानमंत्री <b>महमूद गवाँ</b> ने प्रशासन सुधारा, राज्य को आठ तरफ में विभाजित किया तथा बीदर में मदरसा स्थापित किया।<br>• 1481 में गवाँ के वध के बाद साम्राज्य का पतन हुआ और वह <b>पाँच दक्कन सल्तनतों – बीजापुर, गोलकुंडा, अहमदनगर, बीदर तथा बेरार</b> में बँट गया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि यूरोपीय शक्तियों के साथ व्यापक समुद्री व्यापार वाला कथन गलत है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070623","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The word ‘caste’ has been derived from which language? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"'जाति' (caste) शब्द किस भाषा से लिया गया है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Portuguese","hi":"पुर्तगाली"},"2":{"en":"Spanish","hi":"स्पेनिश"},"3":{"en":"English","hi":"अंग्रेज़ी"},"4":{"en":"Chinese","hi":"चीनी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Portuguese</b><br>The English word <b>'caste'</b> is derived from the <b>Portuguese word 'casta'</b>, meaning race, lineage or breed, which the Portuguese used in India in the 16th century to describe the hereditary social divisions they observed.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Portuguese navigator <b>Vasco da Gama</b> reached India in 1498, and Portuguese writers were the first Europeans to describe Indian social groups as 'castas'.<br>• The Indian terms are <b>'varna'</b>, the four-fold textual classification, and <b>'jati'</b>, the local endogamous birth group.<br>• The caste system was described by <b>H.H. Risley</b> and analysed by sociologists such as M.N. Srinivas, who gave the concept of <b>Sanskritisation</b>.<br>• Portuguese also gave English words such as <b>'caste', 'peon' and 'mango'</b> from Indian languages.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because 'caste' comes from the Portuguese 'casta'.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पुर्तगाली</b><br>अंग्रेज़ी शब्द <b>'caste'</b> <b>पुर्तगाली शब्द 'casta'</b> से बना है, जिसका अर्थ वंश, वंशावली या नस्ल है और जिसे पुर्तगालियों ने 16वीं शताब्दी में भारत में देखे गए वंशानुगत सामाजिक विभाजनों के लिए प्रयोग किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पुर्तगाली नाविक <b>वास्को द गामा</b> 1498 में भारत पहुँचा, और पुर्तगाली लेखक पहले यूरोपीय थे जिन्होंने भारतीय सामाजिक समूहों को 'कास्ता' कहा।<br>• भारतीय शब्द हैं <b>'वर्ण'</b>, जो शास्त्रीय चतुर्विध वर्गीकरण है, तथा <b>'जाति'</b>, जो स्थानीय अंतर्विवाही जन्म-समूह है।<br>• जाति व्यवस्था का वर्णन <b>एच. एच. रिस्ले</b> ने किया और एम. एन. श्रीनिवास जैसे समाजशास्त्रियों ने विश्लेषण किया, जिन्होंने <b>संस्कृतिकरण</b> की अवधारणा दी।<br>• पुर्तगाली भाषा से अंग्रेज़ी में <b>'caste', 'peon' तथा 'mango'</b> जैसे शब्द भी आए।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि 'caste' पुर्तगाली 'casta' से आया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070624","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"______ falls exclusively under the Union List. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"______ पूर्णतः संघ सूची के अंतर्गत आता है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Forests","hi":"वन"},"2":{"en":"Foreign Affairs","hi":"विदेशी मामले"},"3":{"en":"Labour","hi":"श्रम"},"4":{"en":"Public Welfare","hi":"लोक कल्याण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Foreign Affairs</b><br><b>Foreign affairs</b> falls exclusively under the <b>Union List</b> (Entry 10), on which only Parliament can legislate, reflecting the need for a single national policy in external relations.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Seventh Schedule has three lists – the <b>Union List (97 entries), State List (61 entries) and Concurrent List (47 entries)</b>; residuary powers rest with Parliament under Article 248.<br>• <b>Foreign affairs, defence, atomic energy, currency and coinage, banking, railways and inter-state migration</b> are Union List subjects.<br>• <b>Forests</b> were shifted from the State List to the <b>Concurrent List</b> by the 42nd Amendment in 1976, and <b>labour and public welfare</b> are also Concurrent List subjects.<br>• Union List subjects reflect the principle of <b>national unity and uniformity</b>, while state subjects protect local diversity.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because foreign affairs falls exclusively under the Union List.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विदेशी मामले</b><br><b>विदेशी मामले</b> पूर्णतः <b>संघ सूची</b> (प्रविष्टि 10) के अंतर्गत आते हैं, जिस पर केवल संसद विधान बना सकती है, क्योंकि बाह्य संबंधों में एकल राष्ट्रीय नीति आवश्यक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सातवीं अनुसूची में तीन सूचियाँ हैं – <b>संघ सूची (97 प्रविष्टियाँ), राज्य सूची (61 प्रविष्टियाँ) तथा समवर्ती सूची (47 प्रविष्टियाँ)</b>; अवशिष्ट शक्तियाँ अनुच्छेद 248 के अंतर्गत संसद के पास हैं।<br>• <b>विदेशी मामले, रक्षा, परमाणु ऊर्जा, मुद्रा एवं सिक्के, बैंकिंग, रेल तथा अंतर-राज्यीय प्रवासन</b> संघ सूची के विषय हैं।<br>• <b>वन</b> को 1976 के 42वें संशोधन द्वारा राज्य सूची से <b>समवर्ती सूची</b> में स्थानांतरित किया गया, और <b>श्रम तथा लोक कल्याण</b> भी समवर्ती सूची के विषय हैं।<br>• संघ सूची के विषय <b>राष्ट्रीय एकता एवं एकरूपता</b> के सिद्धांत को तथा राज्य के विषय स्थानीय विविधता को प्रकट करते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि विदेशी मामले पूर्णतः संघ सूची के अंतर्गत आते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070625","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The T12 classification in Paralympic athletics is designated for athletes with: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पैरालंपिक एथलेटिक्स में T12 वर्गीकरण किन खिलाड़ियों के लिए निर्धारित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Complete vision loss","hi":"पूर्ण दृष्टिहीनता"},"2":{"en":"Partial visual impairment","hi":"आंशिक दृष्टि दोष"},"3":{"en":"Intellectual disability","hi":"बौद्धिक अक्षमता"},"4":{"en":"Upper limb amputation","hi":"ऊपरी अंग का विच्छेदन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Partial visual impairment</b><br>In <b>Para athletics</b>, the <b>T12</b> class is meant for athletes with <b>partial visual impairment</b> – a very low level of vision – who compete with a guide runner or with visual aids as permitted.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The vision impairment classes are <b>T11 (no vision), T12 (partial vision) and T13 (least severe visual impairment)</b>.<br>• The letter <b>'T'</b> denotes track events and <b>'F'</b> field events, so F12 applies to throwers and jumpers in the same class.<br>• Athletes in T11 usually run with a <b>guide runner</b>, while T12 and T13 athletes may compete with a guide depending on classification.<br>• <b>T20</b> is for athletes with intellectual disability, and upper limb amputees are classified in the <b>T45-T47</b> and similar classes.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because T12 is for athletes with partial visual impairment.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – आंशिक दृष्टि दोष</b><br><b>पैरा एथलेटिक्स</b> में <b>T12</b> वर्ग उन खिलाड़ियों के लिए है जिनमें <b>आंशिक दृष्टि दोष</b> अर्थात दृष्टि का अत्यंत निम्न स्तर है और जो अनुमत सीमा तक गाइड धावक या दृष्टि सहायक उपकरणों के साथ प्रतिस्पर्धा करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दृष्टि दोष वर्ग हैं – <b>T11 (दृष्टि नहीं), T12 (आंशिक दृष्टि) तथा T13 (सबसे कम गंभीर दृष्टि दोष)</b>।<br>• अक्षर <b>'T'</b> ट्रैक स्पर्धाओं तथा <b>'F'</b> फील्ड स्पर्धाओं को दर्शाता है, इसलिए इसी वर्ग के थ्रोअर एवं जंपर के लिए F12 लागू होता है।<br>• T11 के खिलाड़ी सामान्यतः <b>गाइड धावक</b> के साथ दौड़ते हैं, जबकि T12 तथा T13 खिलाड़ी वर्गीकरण के अनुसार गाइड के साथ प्रतिस्पर्धा कर सकते हैं।<br>• <b>T20</b> बौद्धिक अक्षमता वाले खिलाड़ियों के लिए है, तथा ऊपरी अंग विच्छेदन वाले खिलाड़ी <b>T45-T47</b> जैसे वर्गों में आते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि T12 आंशिक दृष्टि दोष वाले खिलाड़ियों के लिए है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070626","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Which pollutant is primarily responsible for the formation of acid rain? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अम्ल वर्षा के निर्माण के लिए मुख्य रूप से कौन-सा प्रदूषक उत्तरदायी है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Carbon dioxide","hi":"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड"},"2":{"en":"Sulfur dioxide","hi":"सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड"},"3":{"en":"Methane","hi":"मीथेन"},"4":{"en":"Ozone","hi":"ओज़ोन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sulfur dioxide</b><br><b>Sulfur dioxide (SO₂)</b> is the pollutant primarily responsible for <b>acid rain</b>, as it reacts in the atmosphere to form <b>sulfuric acid</b>; nitrogen oxides also contribute by forming nitric acid.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Acid rain is defined as precipitation with <b>pH below 5.6</b>, and it damages soils, crops, buildings and aquatic life.<br>• The main sources of SO₂ are the <b>burning of coal and oil in thermal power plants and industries</b> and metal smelting.<br>• Control measures include <b>flue gas desulphurisation, use of low-sulphur fuel and scrubbers</b>.<br>• <b>Carbon dioxide and methane</b> are greenhouse gases causing warming, and ozone in the stratosphere shields ultraviolet radiation; ozone at ground level is a pollutant but not the main cause of acid rain.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because sulfur dioxide is primarily responsible for acid rain.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड</b><br><b>सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड (SO₂)</b> <b>अम्ल वर्षा</b> के लिए मुख्य रूप से उत्तरदायी प्रदूषक है, क्योंकि यह वायुमंडल में अभिक्रिया करके <b>सल्फ्यूरिक अम्ल</b> बनाता है; नाइट्रोजन ऑक्साइड भी नाइट्रिक अम्ल बनाकर योगदान देते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अम्ल वर्षा <b>5.6 से कम pH</b> वाली वर्षा है, जो मृदा, फसलों, भवनों तथा जलीय जीवन को हानि पहुँचाती है।<br>• SO₂ के मुख्य स्रोत <b>ताप विद्युत संयंत्रों और उद्योगों में कोयला एवं तेल का दहन</b> तथा धातु गलाना हैं।<br>• नियंत्रण उपायों में <b>फ्लू गैस डीसल्फराइजेशन, कम सल्फर वाले ईंधन का उपयोग तथा स्क्रबर</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• <b>कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड तथा मीथेन</b> ग्रीनहाउस गैसें हैं जो ऊष्मीकरण करती हैं, तथा समतापमंडलीय ओज़ोन पराबैंगनी विकिरण से रक्षा करती है; भूमि-स्तरीय ओज़ोन प्रदूषक है, परंतु अम्ल वर्षा का मुख्य कारण नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि अम्ल वर्षा के लिए मुख्य रूप से सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड उत्तरदायी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070627","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What policy initiative helps improve local manufacturing capacity through specialization at the district level? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सी नीतिगत पहल जिला स्तर पर विशेषीकरण के माध्यम से स्थानीय विनिर्माण क्षमता सुधारने में सहायक है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Make in India","hi":"मेक इन इंडिया"},"2":{"en":"BharatNet","hi":"भारतनेट"},"3":{"en":"One District One Product (ODOP)","hi":"एक जिला एक उत्पाद (ODOP)"},"4":{"en":"Skill India","hi":"स्किल इंडिया"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – One District One Product (ODOP)</b><br>The <b>One District One Product (ODOP)</b> initiative promotes <b>specialisation at the district level</b> by identifying and supporting one distinctive product per district, thereby improving local manufacturing capacity, branding and exports.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• ODOP was launched in <b>Uttar Pradesh in 2018</b> and has been adopted by several states and supported by the central government through the <b>ODOP-Central Sector Scheme</b> under the Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade.<br>• In Uttar Pradesh it covers 75 districts, including <b>Bhadohi carpets, Kannauj perfume, Aligarh locks and Firozabad glass</b>.<br>• The scheme supports <b>MSMEs, artisans and clusters</b> through common facility centres, marketing support and credit.<br>• <b>Make in India</b> is a broad national manufacturing initiative, <b>BharatNet</b> provides rural broadband and <b>Skill India</b> focuses on skilling.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because ODOP promotes district-level specialisation for local manufacturing.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – एक जिला एक उत्पाद (ODOP)</b><br><b>एक जिला एक उत्पाद (ODOP)</b> पहल प्रत्येक जिले के लिए एक विशिष्ट उत्पाद की पहचान एवं सहायता करके <b>जिला स्तर पर विशेषीकरण</b> को बढ़ावा देती है, जिससे स्थानीय विनिर्माण क्षमता, ब्रांडिंग तथा निर्यात सुधरते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ODOP <b>2018 में उत्तर प्रदेश</b> में शुरू हुई और इसे कई राज्यों ने अपनाया तथा केंद्र सरकार ने उद्योग संवर्धन एवं आंतरिक व्यापार विभाग के अंतर्गत <b>ODOP-केंद्रीय क्षेत्र योजना</b> से सहारा दिया।<br>• उत्तर प्रदेश में यह 75 जिलों को समेटती है, जैसे <b>भदोही के कालीन, कन्नौज की इत्र, अलीगढ़ के ताले तथा फिरोजाबाद का काँच</b>।<br>• योजना <b>MSME, शिल्पकारों तथा क्लस्टरों</b> को साझा सुविधा केंद्र, विपणन सहायता एवं ऋण के माध्यम से सहारा देती है।<br>• <b>मेक इन इंडिया</b> व्यापक राष्ट्रीय विनिर्माण पहल है, <b>भारतनेट</b> ग्रामीण ब्रॉडबैंड देता है तथा <b>स्किल इंडिया</b> कौशल पर केंद्रित है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि ODOP स्थानीय विनिर्माण हेतु जिला-स्तरीय विशेषीकरण को बढ़ावा देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070628","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which 2024 event underscored the vitality of South Indian temple traditions? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस 2024 की घटना ने दक्षिण भारतीय मंदिर परंपराओं की जीवंतता को रेखांकित किया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Puducherry Heritage Festival","hi":"पुदुच्चेरी हेरिटेज फेस्टिवल"},"2":{"en":"Kumbhabhishekam ceremonies","hi":"कुंभाभिषेकम समारोह"},"3":{"en":"AR-guided tours of Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई के AR-निर्देशित भ्रमण"},"4":{"en":"Virtual Gandhara museum launch","hi":"वर्चुअल गांधार संग्रहालय का शुभारंभ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Kumbhabhishekam ceremonies</b><br>Several <b>Kumbhabhishekam</b> consecration ceremonies held in <b>2024</b> – including those at major temples in Tamil Nadu and Andhra Pradesh – underscored the continuing vitality of <b>South Indian temple traditions</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Kumbhabhishekam</b> is the ritual consecration (Mahakumbhabhishekam) performed to purify and re-energise a temple, its deities and the kalashas on the vimana, usually after renovation.<br>• South Indian temples follow the <b>Agama shastra</b> texts for rituals, and the ceremony involves Vedic chanting, homams and processions.<br>• Famous examples include the consecrations at <b>Tirumala, Meenakshi temple, Srirangam and Rameswaram</b> temples.<br>• The other options refer to cultural festivals, digital heritage projects or museum launches, not temple consecration traditions.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Kumbhabhishekam ceremonies highlighted South Indian temple traditions in 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कुंभाभिषेकम समारोह</b><br><b>2024</b> में आयोजित अनेक <b>कुंभाभिषेकम</b> प्रतिष्ठा समारोहों – जिनमें तमिलनाडु तथा आंध्र प्रदेश के प्रमुख मंदिरों के समारोह सम्मिलित थे – ने <b>दक्षिण भारतीय मंदिर परंपराओं</b> की जीवंतता को रेखांकित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कुंभाभिषेकम</b> वह अनुष्ठानिक प्रतिष्ठा (महाकुंभाभिषेकम) है जो मंदिर, उसके देवताओं तथा विमान के कलशों को शुद्ध एवं पुनः ऊर्जस्वित करने के लिए, सामान्यतः जीर्णोद्धार के बाद किया जाता है।<br>• दक्षिण भारतीय मंदिर अनुष्ठानों हेतु <b>आगम शास्त्र</b> ग्रंथों का पालन करते हैं, और समारोह में वैदिक मंत्रोच्चार, हवन तथा शोभायात्रा होती है।<br>• प्रसिद्ध उदाहरणों में <b>तिरुमला, मीनाक्षी मंदिर, श्रीरंगम तथा रामेश्वरम</b> मंदिरों के कुंभाभिषेकम सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• अन्य विकल्प सांस्कृतिक उत्सवों, डिजिटल धरोहर परियोजनाओं या संग्रहालय शुभारंभों से संबंधित हैं, मंदिर प्रतिष्ठा परंपरा से नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि कुंभाभिषेकम समारोहों ने 2024 में दक्षिण भारतीय मंदिर परंपराओं को रेखांकित किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070629","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"The compositions of Tyagaraja, Muthuswami Dikshitar, and Syama Sastri are foundational to which tradition? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"त्यागराज, मुथुस्वामी दीक्षितार तथा श्याम शास्त्री की रचनाएँ किस परंपरा की आधारशिला हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hindustani","hi":"हिंदुस्तानी"},"2":{"en":"Bhajan","hi":"भजन"},"3":{"en":"Folk","hi":"लोक"},"4":{"en":"Carnatic","hi":"कर्नाटक"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Carnatic</b><br>The compositions of <b>Tyagaraja, Muthuswami Dikshitar and Syama Sastri</b>, the <b>'Trinity of Carnatic music'</b>, are foundational to the <b>Carnatic</b> (South Indian classical) tradition.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The three composers lived in <b>Tiruvaiyaru, Tamil Nadu</b> in the 18th-19th centuries and composed mainly in <b>Telugu and Sanskrit</b>.<br>• Tyagaraja's <b>Pancharatna kritis</b> are sung at the Tiruvaiyaru Aradhana festival every year.<br>• Carnatic music is built on <b>raga and tala</b>, with forms such as <b>varnam, kriti, ragam-tanam-pallavi and tillana</b>.<br>• Hindustani music's foundational figures are different – <b>Amir Khusrau, Tansen, Sadarang and others</b>, with forms such as dhrupad and khayal.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the Trinity's compositions are foundational to Carnatic music.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – कर्नाटक</b><br><b>'कर्नाटक संगीत की त्रिमूर्ति'</b> कहे जाने वाले <b>त्यागराज, मुथुस्वामी दीक्षितार तथा श्याम शास्त्री</b> की रचनाएँ <b>कर्नाटक</b> (दक्षिण भारतीय शास्त्रीय) परंपरा की आधारशिला हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तीनों संगीतकार 18वीं-19वीं शताब्दी में <b>तिरुवैयारु, तमिलनाडु</b> में रहे और मुख्यतः <b>तेलुगु तथा संस्कृत</b> में रचनाएँ कीं।<br>• त्यागराज की <b>पंचरत्न कृतियाँ</b> प्रतिवर्ष तिरुवैयारु आराधना उत्सव में गाई जाती हैं।<br>• कर्नाटक संगीत <b>राग तथा ताल</b> पर आधारित है, जिसके रूप <b>वर्णम, कृति, रागम-तानम-पल्लवी तथा तिल्लाना</b> हैं।<br>• हिंदुस्तानी संगीत के आधार-पुरुष भिन्न हैं – <b>अमीर खुसरो, तानसेन, सदारंग आदि</b>, और इसके रूप ध्रुपद एवं खयाल हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि त्रिमूर्ति की रचनाएँ कर्नाटक संगीत की आधारशिला हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070630","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following initiatives focuses on the capacity building of civil servants? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पहल सिविल सेवकों की क्षमता निर्माण पर केंद्रित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mission Antyodaya","hi":"मिशन अंत्योदय"},"2":{"en":"Mission Indradhanush","hi":"मिशन इंद्रधनुष"},"3":{"en":"Mission Karmayogi","hi":"मिशन कर्मयोगी"},"4":{"en":"Mission Shakti","hi":"मिशन शक्ति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Mission Karmayogi</b><br><b>Mission Karmayogi</b> is the National Programme for Civil Services Capacity Building, focused on the <b>capacity building of civil servants</b> through competency-based training, the iGOT platform and institutional reform.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was launched in <b>September 2020</b> and is anchored by the <b>Capacity Building Commission</b> and 'Karmayogi Bharat'.<br>• <b>Mission Antyodaya</b> is a convergence framework for poverty reduction in gram panchayats, and <b>Mission Indradhanush</b> is an immunisation programme.<br>• <b>Mission Shakti</b> covers women's safety and empowerment through the Ministry of Women and Child Development.<br>• Mission Karmayogi aims at making the civil service <b>more creative, citizen-centric and professional</b>, moving from rule-based to role-based training.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Mission Karmayogi focuses on capacity building of civil servants.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – मिशन कर्मयोगी</b><br><b>मिशन कर्मयोगी</b> सिविल सेवा क्षमता निर्माण हेतु राष्ट्रीय कार्यक्रम है, जो योग्यता-आधारित प्रशिक्षण, iGOT प्लेटफॉर्म तथा संस्थागत सुधार के माध्यम से <b>सिविल सेवकों की क्षमता निर्माण</b> पर केंद्रित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह <b>सितंबर 2020</b> में शुरू हुआ और इसका आधार <b>क्षमता निर्माण आयोग</b> तथा 'कर्मयोगी भारत' है।<br>• <b>मिशन अंत्योदय</b> ग्राम पंचायतों में गरीबी घटाने की समन्वय रूपरेखा है, और <b>मिशन इंद्रधनुष</b> टीकाकरण कार्यक्रम है।<br>• <b>मिशन शक्ति</b> महिला एवं बाल विकास मंत्रालय के माध्यम से महिलाओं की सुरक्षा तथा सशक्तीकरण से संबंधित है।<br>• मिशन कर्मयोगी सिविल सेवा को <b>अधिक सृजनात्मक, नागरिक-केंद्रित तथा व्यावसायिक</b> बनाना चाहता है और नियम-आधारित से भूमिका-आधारित प्रशिक्षण की ओर बढ़ता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि मिशन कर्मयोगी सिविल सेवकों की क्षमता निर्माण पर केंद्रित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070631","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Which value of m gives a Pythagorean triplet where the difference between the hypotenuse and the middle number is 2? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"m का कौन-सा मान एक पाइथागोरस त्रिक देता है जिसमें कर्ण और मध्य संख्या का अंतर 2 है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"With m = 3, the triplet formed is 6, 8, 10<br>Check: \\(6^2 + 8^2 = 36 + 64 = 100 = 10^2\\) ✓<br>Hypotenuse − middle number \\(= 10 - 8 = 2\\), exactly the required gap<br>Hence \\(m = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"\\(m = 3\\) के लिए त्रिक 6, 8, 10 बनता है<br>जाँच: \\(6^2 + 8^2 = 36 + 64 = 100 = 10^2\\) ✓<br>कर्ण − मध्य संख्या \\(= 10 - 8 = 2\\), ठीक अभीष्ट अंतर<br>इसलिए \\(m = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070632","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A flat valued at ₹5,00,000 appreciates annually at a rate of 8% compound interest. In how many full years will its value become at least ₹6,80,250? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹5,00,000 मूल्य का एक फ्लैट 8% चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज की वार्षिक दर से मूल्यवृद्धि पाता है। कितने पूर्ण वर्षों में उसका मूल्य कम से कम ₹6,80,250 हो जाएगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 years","hi":"3 वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"4 years","hi":"4 वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"5 years","hi":"5 वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"6 years","hi":"6 वर्ष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Amount after n years \\(= 5{,}00{,}000(1.08)^n\\)<br>n = 2 gives \\(5{,}83{,}200\\) and n = 3 gives \\(5{,}00{,}000 \\times 1.08^3 = 6{,}29{,}856\\), both below ₹6,80,250<br>n = 4 gives \\(5{,}00{,}000 \\times 1.08^4 = 6{,}80{,}244.48 \\approx 6{,}80{,}245\\), which is the required ₹6,80,250 (to the nearest rupee the printed target is reached here)<br>So the value becomes at least ₹6,80,250 in \\(\\boxed{4}\\) full years<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4 years.</b>","hi":"n वर्षों बाद राशि \\(= 5{,}00{,}000(1.08)^n\\)<br>n = 2 पर \\(5{,}83{,}200\\) तथा n = 3 पर \\(5{,}00{,}000 \\times 1.08^3 = 6{,}29{,}856\\) मिलता है, दोनों ₹6,80,250 से कम हैं<br>n = 4 पर \\(5{,}00{,}000 \\times 1.08^4 = 6{,}80{,}244.48 \\approx 6{,}80{,}245\\) मिलता है, जो अपेक्षित ₹6,80,250 है (निकटतम रुपये तक पूर्णांकन पर)<br>अतः मूल्य \\(\\boxed{4}\\) पूर्ण वर्षों में कम से कम ₹6,80,250 हो जाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 वर्ष है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070633","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A vendor invests the same cost price in two items, each costing ₹40,000. He sells one item at a 25% profit and the other at a 25% loss. The average selling price of the two items becomes the principal invested in a 2-year compound interest scheme at 10% per annum. Using algebraic identities, what is the compound interest earned on this investment? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक विक्रेता दो वस्तुओं में समान लागत मूल्य निवेश करता है, जिनमें से प्रत्येक का मूल्य ₹40,000 है। वह एक वस्तु 25% लाभ पर और दूसरी 25% हानि पर बेचता है। दोनों वस्तुओं का औसत विक्रय मूल्य 10% प्रति वर्ष की दर से 2 वर्ष की चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज योजना में निवेश की गई मूलधन राशि बन जाता है। बीजगणितीय सर्वसमिकाओं का प्रयोग करते हुए इस निवेश पर अर्जित चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹8,500"},"2":{"en":"₹8,000"},"3":{"en":"₹8,025"},"4":{"en":"₹8,400"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"SP of the two items: \\(40{,}000 \\times 1.25 = 50{,}000\\) and \\(40{,}000 \\times 0.75 = 30{,}000\\)<br>Average SP \\(= \\frac{50{,}000 + 30{,}000}{2} = 40{,}000\\) (identity: 25% gain and 25% loss cancel)<br>CI \\(= 40{,}000\\left[(1.1)^2 - 1\\right] = 40{,}000 \\times 0.21\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹8,400.</b>","hi":"दोनों वस्तुओं का विक्रय मूल्य: \\(40{,}000 \\times 1.25 = 50{,}000\\) और \\(40{,}000 \\times 0.75 = 30{,}000\\)<br>औसत विक्रय मूल्य \\(= \\frac{50{,}000 + 30{,}000}{2} = 40{,}000\\) (सर्वसमिका: 25% लाभ और 25% हानि एक-दूसरे को काट देते हैं)<br>चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज \\(= 40{,}000\\left[(1.1)^2 - 1\\right] = 40{,}000 \\times 0.21\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹8,400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070634","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"Consider a triangle ABC with vertices A(0, 0), B(8, 0) and C(4, 6). Which of the following statements about its centers is false? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शीर्षों A(0, 0), B(8, 0) और C(4, 6) वाले त्रिभुज ABC पर विचार कीजिए। इसके केंद्रों के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन असत्य है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The centroid is located at (4, 2).","hi":"केंद्रक (4, 2) पर स्थित है।"},"2":{"en":"The orthocenter lies inside the triangle.","hi":"लंबकेंद्र त्रिभुज के भीतर स्थित है।"},"3":{"en":"The circumcenter is equidistant from A, B, and C.","hi":"परिकेंद्र A, B और C से समान दूरी पर है।"},"4":{"en":"The incenter is equidistant from the midpoints of the sides AB, BC, CA.","hi":"अंतःकेंद्र भुजाओं AB, BC, CA के मध्य-बिंदुओं से समान दूरी पर है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Centroid \\(= \\left(\\frac{0+8+4}{3}, \\frac{0+0+6}{3}\\right) = (4, 2)\\) ✓<br>AB = 8, AC = BC = \\(\\sqrt{16+36} = \\sqrt{52}\\), so the triangle is isosceles and acute, hence the orthocenter lies inside ✓<br>The circumcenter is equidistant from the vertices ✓<br>But the incenter is equidistant from the <i>sides</i>, not from their midpoints ✗<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\text{The incenter is equidistant from the midpoints of the sides AB, BC, CA.}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The incenter is equidistant from the midpoints of the sides AB, BC, CA.</b>","hi":"केंद्रक \\(= \\left(\\frac{0+8+4}{3}, \\frac{0+0+6}{3}\\right) = (4, 2)\\) ✓<br>AB = 8, AC = BC = \\(\\sqrt{16+36} = \\sqrt{52}\\), अतः त्रिभुज समद्विबाहु और न्यूनकोण है, इसलिए लंबकेंद्र भीतर है ✓<br>परिकेंद्र शीर्षों से समान दूरी पर होता है ✓<br>परंतु अंतःकेंद्र <i>भुजाओं</i> से समान दूरी पर होता है, उनके मध्य-बिंदुओं से नहीं ✗<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\text{अंतःकेंद्र भुजाओं AB, BC, CA के मध्य-बिंदुओं से समान दूरी पर है।}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): अंतःकेंद्र भुजाओं AB, BC, CA के मध्य-बिंदुओं से समान दूरी पर है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070635","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If x³ + y³ + z³ = 3xyz + 6, and let L = x − y − z, M = y − z − x, N = z − x − y, then find the value of L³ + M³ + N³ − 3LMN. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि x³ + y³ + z³ = 3xyz + 6 है, और L = x − y − z, M = y − z − x, N = z − x − y लीजिए, तो L³ + M³ + N³ − 3LMN का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"−24"},"2":{"en":"−18"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"18"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Put s = x + y + z, then L = 2x − s, M = 2y − s, N = 2z − s<br>So L + M + N = −s, and \\(L^2 + M^2 + N^2 - LM - MN - NL = 2[(x-y)^2 + (y-z)^2 + (z-x)^2]\\)<br>The given condition \\(x^3 + y^3 + z^3 - 3xyz = 6\\) gives \\(s[(x-y)^2 + (y-z)^2 + (z-x)^2] = 12\\)<br>Therefore \\(L^3 + M^3 + N^3 - 3LMN = -2 \\times 12 = \\boxed{-24}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): −24.</b>","hi":"s = x + y + z रखिए, तब L = 2x − s, M = 2y − s, N = 2z − s<br>अतः L + M + N = −s, और \\(L^2 + M^2 + N^2 - LM - MN - NL = 2[(x-y)^2 + (y-z)^2 + (z-x)^2]\\)<br>दी गई शर्त \\(x^3 + y^3 + z^3 - 3xyz = 6\\) से \\(s[(x-y)^2 + (y-z)^2 + (z-x)^2] = 12\\)<br>इसलिए \\(L^3 + M^3 + N^3 - 3LMN = -2 \\times 12 = \\boxed{-24}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): −24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070636","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Due to headwind, a drone took 2 hours to fly from City A to City B and 3 hours to return. If 72 km/h was the average speed for the entire journey, what was the distance (one way) between the two cities? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"प्रतिकूल हवा के कारण एक ड्रोन को शहर A से शहर B तक उड़ने में 2 घंटे और वापस आने में 3 घंटे लगे। यदि पूरी यात्रा की औसत चाल 72 km/घंटा थी, तो दोनों शहरों के बीच की दूरी (एक ओर) क्या थी? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"160 km"},"2":{"en":"170 km"},"3":{"en":"180 km"},"4":{"en":"200 km"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the one-way distance be \\(d\\) km<br>Total distance \\(= 2d\\), total time \\(= 2 + 3 = 5\\) hours<br>Average speed \\(= \\frac{2d}{5} = 72\\)<br>\\(2d = 360 \\Rightarrow d = \\boxed{180}\\) km<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 180 km.</b>","hi":"एक ओर की दूरी \\(d\\) km मानिए<br>कुल दूरी \\(= 2d\\), कुल समय \\(= 2 + 3 = 5\\) घंटे<br>औसत चाल \\(= \\frac{2d}{5} = 72\\)<br>\\(2d = 360 \\Rightarrow d = \\boxed{180}\\) km<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 180 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070637","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A can finish 30% of a task in 9 days, B can complete 2/5 of the same task in 10 days, C can do 1/6 of it in 5 days, and D can complete 50% of the task in 12 days. Who among them is the fastest to complete the entire work individually? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"A किसी कार्य का 30% भाग 9 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है, B उसी कार्य का 2/5 भाग 10 दिनों में, C उसका 1/6 भाग 5 दिनों में और D कार्य का 50% भाग 12 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है। उनमें से कौन अकेले पूरा कार्य सबसे तेज़ी से कर सकता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A: 100% in \\(\\frac{9}{0.30} = 30\\) days<br>B: 100% in \\(10 \\times \\frac{5}{2} = 25\\) days<br>C: 100% in \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\) days<br>D: 100% in \\(12 \\times 2 = 24\\) days<br>The least time is D's, so \\(\\boxed{D}\\) is the fastest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): D.</b>","hi":"A: 100% कार्य \\(\\frac{9}{0.30} = 30\\) दिनों में<br>B: 100% कार्य \\(10 \\times \\frac{5}{2} = 25\\) दिनों में<br>C: 100% कार्य \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\) दिनों में<br>D: 100% कार्य \\(12 \\times 2 = 24\\) दिनों में<br>न्यूनतम समय D का है, अतः \\(\\boxed{D}\\) सबसे तेज़ है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070638","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A textile factory has two machines, M1 and M2, that process fabric rolls. M1 can complete a batch in 18 days, and M2 in 12 days. Both machines are scheduled to work alternate days, starting with M1 on Day 1. Due to quality checks, only 80% of M1's work and 90% of M2's work is accepted. Assuming the cycle continues until the entire batch (LCM of their working days) is accepted, in how many total days will the work be completed? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वस्त्र कारखाने में दो मशीनें M1 और M2 कपड़े के रोल तैयार करती हैं। M1 एक बैच 18 दिनों में और M2 12 दिनों में पूरा कर सकती है। दोनों मशीनें बारी-बारी से कार्य करती हैं, जिसमें दिन 1 पर M1 प्रारंभ करती है। गुणवत्ता जाँच के कारण M1 के कार्य का केवल 80% और M2 के कार्य का केवल 90% स्वीकार किया जाता है। यदि चक्र तब तक चलता है जब तक पूरा बैच स्वीकार न हो जाए, तो कुल कितने दिनों में कार्य पूरा होगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17 days","hi":"17 दिन"},"2":{"en":"18 days","hi":"18 दिन"},"3":{"en":"19 days","hi":"19 दिन"},"4":{"en":"20 days","hi":"20 दिन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Accepted work of M1 per working day \\(= \\frac{0.8}{18} = \\frac{2}{45}\\)<br>Accepted work of M2 per working day \\(= \\frac{0.9}{12} = \\frac{3}{40}\\)<br>Work accepted in one 2-day cycle \\(= \\frac{2}{45} + \\frac{3}{40} = \\frac{16 + 27}{360} = \\frac{43}{360}\\)<br>In 8 cycles (16 days) the accepted work is \\(\\frac{344}{360}\\), leaving \\(\\frac{16}{360} = \\frac{2}{45}\\)<br>On day 17 machine M1 alone gives only \\(\\frac{2}{45}\\) of accepted work, so the batch is completed at the end of day 17<br>Total days \\(= \\boxed{17}\\) (day 17 with M1 completing the balance exactly)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 17 days.</b>","hi":"प्रति कार्य-दिवस M1 का स्वीकृत कार्य \\(= \\frac{0.8}{18} = \\frac{2}{45}\\)<br>प्रति कार्य-दिवस M2 का स्वीकृत कार्य \\(= \\frac{0.9}{12} = \\frac{3}{40}\\)<br>एक 2-दिन के चक्र में स्वीकृत कार्य \\(= \\frac{2}{45} + \\frac{3}{40} = \\frac{16 + 27}{360} = \\frac{43}{360}\\)<br>8 चक्रों (16 दिन) में स्वीकृत कार्य \\(\\frac{344}{360}\\) है, शेष \\(\\frac{16}{360} = \\frac{2}{45}\\) बचता है<br>17वें दिन M1 अकेले \\(\\frac{2}{45}\\) स्वीकृत कार्य करती है, इसलिए बैच 17वें दिन के अंत में पूरा हो जाता है<br>कुल दिन \\(= \\boxed{17}\\) (17वें दिन M1 शेष कार्य पूरा करती है)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 17 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070639","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A tangent is drawn to a circle at point T. From a point A on the circle, a chord AB is drawn parallel to the tangent. If the length of the chord AB = 16 cm and the radius of the circle is 10 cm, find the distance from point T to the chord AB. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त पर बिंदु T से स्पर्श रेखा खींची गई है। वृत्त पर स्थित बिंदु A से स्पर्श रेखा के समांतर जीवा AB खींची गई है। यदि जीवा AB की लंबाई 16 cm और वृत्त की त्रिज्या 10 cm है, तो बिंदु T से जीवा AB की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21 cm"},"2":{"en":"3 cm"},"3":{"en":"7 cm"},"4":{"en":"4 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 170L188 170M116 116L116 170M123 170L123 163L116 163M35 206L197 206\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 116L188 170M116 170L116 206\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"110\">O</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">6</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"11\">8</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"155\">10</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"217\">T</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">4</text></g></svg><br>The radius OT is perpendicular to the tangent, so the distance from the centre to the parallel chord is \\(\\sqrt{10^2 - 8^2} = 6\\) cm<br>Since the chord is parallel to the tangent (on the same side as T's contact), the distance from T to the chord \\(= 10 - 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 170L188 170M116 116L116 170M123 170L123 163L116 163M35 206L197 206\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 116L188 170M116 170L116 206\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"110\">O</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">6</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"11\">8</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"155\">10</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"217\">T</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">4</text></g></svg><br>त्रिज्या OT स्पर्श रेखा के लंबवत है, अतः केंद्र से समांतर जीवा की दूरी \\(\\sqrt{10^2 - 8^2} = 6\\) cm<br>जीवा स्पर्श रेखा के समांतर है, अतः T से जीवा की दूरी \\(= 10 - 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070640","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"For a cylinder with a radius to height ratio of 5:6, if its curved surface area is 660π, find the radius. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"5:6 त्रिज्या-से-ऊँचाई अनुपात वाले एक बेलन का वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 660π है, तो त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{10}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{11}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{11}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{10}\\) cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"203\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 203 190\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 140A75 24 0 0 0 176 140M26 140L26 50M176 140L176 50\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 140A75 24 0 0 1 176 140M101 50L176 50\"/><ellipse cx=\"101\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"24\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"11\">5k</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"99\">6k</text></g></svg><br>Let \\(r = 5k\\), \\(h = 6k\\)<br>\\(2\\pi rh = 2\\pi(5k)(6k) = 60\\pi k^2 = 660\\pi\\)<br>\\(k^2 = 11 \\Rightarrow k = \\sqrt{11}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{5\\sqrt{11}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(5\\sqrt{11}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"203\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 203 190\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 140A75 24 0 0 0 176 140M26 140L26 50M176 140L176 50\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 140A75 24 0 0 1 176 140M101 50L176 50\"/><ellipse cx=\"101\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"75\" ry=\"24\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"11\">5k</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"99\">6k</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = 5k\\), \\(h = 6k\\) मानिए<br>\\(2\\pi rh = 2\\pi(5k)(6k) = 60\\pi k^2 = 660\\pi\\)<br>\\(k^2 = 11 \\Rightarrow k = \\sqrt{11}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{5\\sqrt{11}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(5\\sqrt{11}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070641","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"An equilateral triangle, having a side measurement of 6 cm, forms the base of a regular right pyramid. Calculate the apothem's length for this base triangle. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"6 cm भुजा वाला एक समबाहु त्रिभुज एक सम न्यूनकोणीय (शीर्षलंब) पिरामिड का आधार बनाता है। इस आधार त्रिभुज के लिए एपोथेम की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(3\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"199\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 199\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M111 26L26 173L196 173ZM111 124L111 173M117 173L117 167L111 167\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"124\" r=\"49\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"184\">B</text><text x=\"209\" y=\"184\">C</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"92\">6 cm</text><text x=\"174\" y=\"92\">6 cm</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"189\">6 cm</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"153\">r</text></g></svg><br>The apothem of an equilateral triangle is the inradius<br>\\(r = \\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"199\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 199\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M111 26L26 173L196 173ZM111 124L111 173M117 173L117 167L111 167\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"124\" r=\"49\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"184\">B</text><text x=\"209\" y=\"184\">C</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"92\">6 cm</text><text x=\"174\" y=\"92\">6 cm</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"189\">6 cm</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"153\">r</text></g></svg><br>समबाहु त्रिभुज का एपोथेम उसका अंतःत्रिज्या है<br>\\(r = \\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070642","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base of a right prism is a trapezoid with parallel sides 12 cm, 20 cm and height 9 cm. If the volume is 3888 cm³, what is the prism's height? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समकोणीय प्रिज्म का आधार 12 cm, 20 cm समांतर भुजाओं और 9 cm ऊँचाई वाला समलंब है। यदि आयतन 3888 cm³ है, तो प्रिज्म की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"29 cm"},"2":{"en":"35 cm"},"3":{"en":"25 cm"},"4":{"en":"27 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"166\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 166 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L140 196M26 42L140 42M26 196L26 42M140 42L131 26M140 196L140 42M131 26L63 26M63 26L26 42\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M140 196L131 180M131 180L63 180M131 180L131 26M63 180L26 196M63 180L63 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"13\" y=\"123\">H</text><text x=\"83\" y=\"212\">20</text><text x=\"97\" y=\"172\">12</text></g></svg><br>Area of the trapezoid base \\(= \\frac{12 + 20}{2} \\times 9 = 16 \\times 9 = 144\\) cm²<br>\\(144 \\times H = 3888\\)<br>\\(H = \\boxed{27}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 27 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"166\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 166 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L140 196M26 42L140 42M26 196L26 42M140 42L131 26M140 196L140 42M131 26L63 26M63 26L26 42\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M140 196L131 180M131 180L63 180M131 180L131 26M63 180L26 196M63 180L63 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"13\" y=\"123\">H</text><text x=\"83\" y=\"212\">20</text><text x=\"97\" y=\"172\">12</text></g></svg><br>समलंब आधार का क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{12 + 20}{2} \\times 9 = 16 \\times 9 = 144\\) cm²<br>\\(144 \\times H = 3888\\)<br>\\(H = \\boxed{27}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 27 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070643","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Simplify: \\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"secθ"},"2":{"en":"tanθ + 1"},"3":{"en":"sinθ + 1"},"4":{"en":"cosθ + 1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\tan\\theta + 1\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\tan\\theta + 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): tanθ + 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\tan\\theta + 1\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\tan\\theta + 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): tanθ + 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070644","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1+\\sin\\theta} = 4\\), then what is the value of θ (in degrees) where 0° < θ < 90°? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1+\\sin\\theta} = 4\\) है, तो θ का मान (डिग्री में) क्या है, जहाँ 0° < θ < 90° है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45°"},"2":{"en":"60°"},"3":{"en":"75°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta) + \\cos\\theta(1 - \\sin\\theta)}{1 - \\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{2\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} = 4 \\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 60°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta) + \\cos\\theta(1 - \\sin\\theta)}{1 - \\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{2\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} = 4 \\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070645","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A container holds 12 litres of pure honey. First, 3 litres are removed and replaced with water. Then, again 3 litres of the new mixture are removed and replaced with water. What is the ratio of honey left in the container to the original quantity? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बर्तन में 12 लीटर शुद्ध शहद है। पहले 3 लीटर निकालकर उसके स्थान पर पानी डाला जाता है। फिर नए मिश्रण के 3 लीटर निकालकर उसके स्थान पर पानी डाला जाता है। बर्तन में बचे शहद और मूल मात्रा का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9 : 16"},"2":{"en":"4 : 9"},"3":{"en":"16 : 25"},"4":{"en":"25 : 36"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Replacement formula: remaining \\(= 12\\left(1 - \\frac{3}{12}\\right)^2 = 12 \\times \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2 = 12 \\times \\frac{9}{16}\\)<br>Honey left \\(= \\frac{27}{4}\\) litres out of 12 litres<br>Ratio \\(= \\frac{9}{16} = \\boxed{9 : 16}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 9 : 16.</b>","hi":"प्रतिस्थापन सूत्र: शेष \\(= 12\\left(1 - \\frac{3}{12}\\right)^2 = 12 \\times \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2 = 12 \\times \\frac{9}{16}\\)<br>बचा शहद 12 लीटर में से \\(\\frac{27}{4}\\) लीटर<br>अनुपात \\(= \\frac{9}{16} = \\boxed{9 : 16}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 9 : 16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070646","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"The ratio between the height of the tower and the point at some distance is 5√3 : 5. What will be the angle of elevation? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मीनार की ऊँचाई और कुछ दूरी पर स्थित बिंदु का अनुपात 5√3 : 5 है। उन्नयन कोण क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40°"},"2":{"en":"60°"},"3":{"en":"15°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"146\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"-7 0 146 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 176L113 176M26 176L26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168M113 176L26 26M95 176A18 18 0 0 1 104 160\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">B</text><text x=\"7\" y=\"105\">5√3</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"11\">θ</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"190\">C</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"192\">5</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\text{height}}{\\text{distance}} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{5} = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 60°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"146\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"-7 0 146 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 176L113 176M26 176L26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168M113 176L26 26M95 176A18 18 0 0 1 104 160\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">B</text><text x=\"7\" y=\"105\">5√3</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"11\">θ</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"190\">C</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"192\">5</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\text{ऊँचाई}}{\\text{दूरी}} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{5} = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070647","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"The graph of which equation passes through the origin? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस समीकरण का ग्राफ मूल बिंदु से गुज़रता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"x + y = 1"},"2":{"en":"x − y = 0"},"3":{"en":"2x + 3 = 0"},"4":{"en":"x = 5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A line passes through the origin if (0, 0) satisfies it<br>\\(0 - 0 = 0\\) ✓ for \\(x - y = 0\\); the others give \\(0 \\ne 1\\), \\(3 \\ne 0\\), \\(0 \\ne 5\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{x - y = 0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): x − y = 0.</b>","hi":"रेखा मूल बिंदु से गुज़रती है यदि (0, 0) उसे संतुष्ट करता है<br>\\(x - y = 0\\) के लिए \\(0 - 0 = 0\\) ✓; अन्य के लिए \\(0 \\ne 1\\), \\(3 \\ne 0\\), \\(0 \\ne 5\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{x - y = 0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): x − y = 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070648","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Factorise: x³ + 8 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गुणनखंड कीजिए: x³ + 8 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(x + 2)(x² + 2x + 4)"},"2":{"en":"(x + 2)(x² − 2x + 4)"},"3":{"en":"(x − 2)(x² + 2x + 4)"},"4":{"en":"(x − 2)(x² − 2x + 4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2)\\) with \\(a = x\\), \\(b = 2\\)<br>\\(x^3 + 8 = \\boxed{(x + 2)(x^2 - 2x + 4)}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (x + 2)(x² − 2x + 4).</b>","hi":"\\(a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2)\\), जहाँ \\(a = x\\), \\(b = 2\\)<br>\\(x^3 + 8 = \\boxed{(x + 2)(x^2 - 2x + 4)}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): (x + 2)(x² − 2x + 4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070649","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Which of the following decimals represents the fraction 11/20? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा दशमलव भिन्न 11/20 को दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.55"},"2":{"en":"0.65"},"3":{"en":"0.75"},"4":{"en":"0.45"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{11}{20} = \\frac{11 \\times 5}{20 \\times 5} = \\frac{55}{100}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.55}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0.55.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{11}{20} = \\frac{11 \\times 5}{20 \\times 5} = \\frac{55}{100}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.55}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0.55 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070650","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cotθ = 1, what is cosec²θ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि cotθ = 1 है, तो cosec²θ क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta = 1 + \\cot^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta = 1 + \\cot^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070651","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The height of a square pyramid is 24 cm and slant height is 25 cm. Find the lateral surface area if base side is unknown. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वर्गाकार पिरामिड की ऊँचाई 24 cm और तिर्यक ऊँचाई 25 cm है। यदि आधार भुजा ज्ञात नहीं है, तो पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"700 cm²"},"2":{"en":"500 cm²"},"3":{"en":"520 cm²"},"4":{"en":"540 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"169\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 169 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L73 26L119 186ZM80 186L80 179L73 179\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M73 26L73 186\"/><circle cx=\"73\" cy=\"186\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"68\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">h = 24 cm</text><text x=\"134\" y=\"99\">l = 25 cm</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"11\">a/2</text></g></svg><br>Half the base side \\(= \\sqrt{25^2 - 24^2} = \\sqrt{49} = 7\\) cm, so the side \\(= 14\\) cm<br>Lateral surface area \\(= 4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times 14 \\times 25 = 2 \\times 350\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{700}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 700 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"169\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 169 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L73 26L119 186ZM80 186L80 179L73 179\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M73 26L73 186\"/><circle cx=\"73\" cy=\"186\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"68\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">h = 24 cm</text><text x=\"134\" y=\"99\">l = 25 cm</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"11\">a/2</text></g></svg><br>आधार भुजा का आधा \\(= \\sqrt{25^2 - 24^2} = \\sqrt{49} = 7\\) cm, अतः भुजा \\(= 14\\) cm<br>पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल \\(= 4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times 14 \\times 25 = 2 \\times 350\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{700}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 700 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070652","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"This histogram represents the weights (in kg) of 45 people in a fitness club.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the club wants to create two groups, light (below 55 kg) and heavy (55 kg and above), how many people fall into each group?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यह हिस्टोग्राम एक फिटनेस क्लब के 45 लोगों के भार (kg में) को दर्शाता है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि क्लब दो समूह बनाना चाहता है — हल्का (55 kg से कम) और भारी (55 kg और अधिक) — तो प्रत्येक समूह में कितने लोग आएंगे?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Light: 25, Heavy: 20","hi":"हल्का: 25, भारी: 20"},"2":{"en":"Light: 20, Heavy: 25","hi":"हल्का: 20, भारी: 25"},"3":{"en":"Light: 30, Heavy: 15","hi":"हल्का: 30, भारी: 15"},"4":{"en":"Light: 15, Heavy: 30","hi":"हल्का: 15, भारी: 30"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the histogram: 40–45 → 5, 45–50 → 8, 50–55 → 12, 55–60 → 10, 60–65 → 7, 65–70 → 3<br>Below 55 kg: \\(5 + 8 + 12 = 25\\)<br>55 kg and above: \\(10 + 7 + 3 = 20\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\text{Light: 25, Heavy: 20}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Light: 25, Heavy: 20.</b>","hi":"हिस्टोग्राम से: 40–45 → 5, 45–50 → 8, 50–55 → 12, 55–60 → 10, 60–65 → 7, 65–70 → 3<br>55 kg से कम: \\(5 + 8 + 12 = 25\\)<br>55 kg और अधिक: \\(10 + 7 + 3 = 20\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\text{हल्का: 25, भारी: 20}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): हल्का: 25, भारी: 20 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070653","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"This histogram represents the weights (in kg) of 45 people in a fitness club.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the club decides to award a prize to the weight interval with people closest to the average weight of the group, which class interval is most likely to receive the prize?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यह हिस्टोग्राम एक फिटनेस क्लब के 45 लोगों के भार (kg में) को दर्शाता है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि क्लब उस भार अंतराल को पुरस्कार देने का निर्णय लेता है जिसके लोग समूह के औसत भार के सबसे निकट हैं, तो किस वर्ग अंतराल को पुरस्कार मिलने की सर्वाधिक संभावना है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45-50 kg"},"2":{"en":"50-55 kg"},"3":{"en":"55-60 kg"},"4":{"en":"60-65 kg"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Mid-points × frequencies: \\(42.5(5) + 47.5(8) + 52.5(12) + 57.5(10) + 62.5(7) + 67.5(3)\\)<br>\\(= 212.5 + 380 + 630 + 575 + 437.5 + 202.5 = 2437.5\\)<br>Mean \\(= \\frac{2437.5}{45} = 54.17\\) kg, which lies in 50–55 kg<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{50-55 \\text{ kg}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 50-55 kg.</b>","hi":"मध्य-बिंदु × बारंबारता: \\(42.5(5) + 47.5(8) + 52.5(12) + 57.5(10) + 62.5(7) + 67.5(3)\\)<br>\\(= 212.5 + 380 + 630 + 575 + 437.5 + 202.5 = 2437.5\\)<br>माध्य \\(= \\frac{2437.5}{45} = 54.17\\) kg, जो 50–55 kg में है<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{50-55 \\text{ kg}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 50-55 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q73.jpg"]}},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070654","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"At Zenith National University, the academic year 2023–2024 concluded with a significant graduation ceremony across its five major departments: Engineering, Medicine, Law, Arts, and Commerce.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If each graduate from Commerce contributes ₹5,000 to the alumni fund, and graduates from other departments contribute ₹4,000 each, what is the total fund collected?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ज़ेनिथ नेशनल यूनिवर्सिटी में शैक्षणिक वर्ष 2023–2024 का समापन इसके पाँच प्रमुख विभागों — इंजीनियरिंग, मेडिसिन, लॉ, आर्ट्स और कॉमर्स — के एक भव्य दीक्षांत समारोह के साथ हुआ।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि कॉमर्स के प्रत्येक स्नातक ₹5,000 तथा अन्य विभागों के प्रत्येक स्नातक ₹4,000 पूर्व छात्र निधि में देते हैं, तो कुल एकत्रित निधि कितनी है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹50,00,000"},"2":{"en":"₹50,30,000"},"3":{"en":"₹49,50,000"},"4":{"en":"₹51,00,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the graph: Engineering 320, Medicine 210, Law 160, Arts 280, Commerce 230<br>Commerce contribution \\(= 230 \\times 5000 = 11{,}50{,}000\\)<br>Others \\(= (320 + 210 + 160 + 280) \\times 4000 = 970 \\times 4000 = 38{,}80{,}000\\)<br>Total \\(= \\boxed{50{,}30{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹50,30,000.</b>","hi":"ग्राफ से: इंजीनियरिंग 320, मेडिसिन 210, लॉ 160, आर्ट्स 280, कॉमर्स 230<br>कॉमर्स से योगदान \\(= 230 \\times 5000 = 11{,}50{,}000\\)<br>अन्य \\(= (320 + 210 + 160 + 280) \\times 4000 = 970 \\times 4000 = 38{,}80{,}000\\)<br>कुल \\(= \\boxed{50{,}30{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹50,30,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg"]}},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070655","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart presents the percentage distribution of the production share of five different crops. Study the pie-chart carefully and answer the question based on the provided data.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>A market analyst wants to re-cluster the chart into three primary economic sectors:<br>1. Sector I (Cereals): Wheat + Rice + Maize<br>2. Sector II (Proteins): Pulses<br>3. Sector III (Miscellaneous): Others<br>Problem: What is the difference between the central angle of Sector I and the combined central angles of Sector II and Sector III?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट पाँच भिन्न फसलों के उत्पादन हिस्से का प्रतिशत वितरण दर्शाता है। पाई-चार्ट को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और दिए गए आँकड़ों के आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>एक बाज़ार विश्लेषक चार्ट को तीन प्रमुख आर्थिक क्षेत्रों में पुनः समूहित करना चाहता है:<br>1. क्षेत्र I (अनाज): गेहूँ + चावल + मक्का<br>2. क्षेत्र II (प्रोटीन): दालें<br>3. क्षेत्र III (विविध): अन्य<br>प्रश्न: क्षेत्र I के केंद्रीय कोण और क्षेत्र II तथा क्षेत्र III के संयुक्त केंद्रीय कोणों का अंतर क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"90°"},"2":{"en":"180°"},"3":{"en":"120°"},"4":{"en":"45°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Wheat 32%, Rice 28%, Maize 15%, Pulses 15%, Others 10%<br>Sector I \\(= 32 + 28 + 15 = 75\\%\\) → central angle \\(= 0.75 \\times 360^\\circ = 270^\\circ\\)<br>Sectors II + III \\(= 15 + 10 = 25\\%\\) → \\(0.25 \\times 360^\\circ = 90^\\circ\\)<br>Difference \\(= 270^\\circ - 90^\\circ = \\boxed{180^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 180°.</b>","hi":"पाई चार्ट से: गेहूँ 32%, चावल 28%, मक्का 15%, दालें 15%, अन्य 10%<br>क्षेत्र I \\(= 32 + 28 + 15 = 75\\%\\) → केंद्रीय कोण \\(= 0.75 \\times 360^\\circ = 270^\\circ\\)<br>क्षेत्र II + III \\(= 15 + 10 = 25\\%\\) → \\(0.25 \\times 360^\\circ = 90^\\circ\\)<br>अंतर \\(= 270^\\circ - 90^\\circ = \\boxed{180^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 180° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg"]}}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070656","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"What is the antonym of the word “lucid”? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bright"},"2":{"en":"Clear"},"3":{"en":"Confused"},"4":{"en":"Transparent"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Lucid (स्पष्ट) = clear and easy to understand.</b><br><b>Bright (तेज)</b> = vivid or intelligent<br><b>Clear (स्पष्ट)</b> = intelligible<br><b>Confused (अस्पष्ट)</b> = unclear ✔<br><b>Transparent (पारदर्शी)</b> = clear.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Confused.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070657","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“By leaps and bounds” [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Slowly"},"2":{"en":"Rapidly and noticeably"},"3":{"en":"Carefully"},"4":{"en":"Through politics"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>By leaps and bounds (तेज़ी से) = very rapidly and substantially.</b><br>Example: “Her language skills improved by leaps and bounds.”<br>Slow progress is the opposite.<br>Care and politics are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Rapidly and noticeably.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070658","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>She is married with a banker (1)/ and has been living in London (2)/ for the past five years (3)/ with her family. (4) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Married to someone” is the standard construction.</b><br>Part (1) should read “She is married <b>to</b> a banker.”<br>“Married with” is unidiomatic.<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070659","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>Although framed as reformist, the policy inadvertently ___ structural inequalities rather than mitigating them. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"perpetuated"},"2":{"en":"repelled"},"3":{"en":"amplified"},"4":{"en":"suppressed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Perpetuate (बनाए रखना) = cause something to continue.</b><br>The policy unintentionally perpetuated inequalities instead of reducing them.<br>“Repelled” means drove away, and “suppressed” means restrained.<br>“Amplified” means intensified but is not the keyed choice.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): perpetuated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070660","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “Once in a blue moon” mean? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Something that happens often"},"2":{"en":"Something that happens daily"},"3":{"en":"Something that happens every year"},"4":{"en":"Something that happens very rarely"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Once in a blue moon (बहुत कभी-कभार) = extremely rarely.</b><br>Example: “We eat out only once in a blue moon.”<br>Frequent, daily and annual events do not convey rarity.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Something that happens very rarely.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070661","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>I wish the report <b>is finished</b> before the meeting began. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"was finishing"},"2":{"en":"has finished"},"3":{"en":"had been finished"},"4":{"en":"finished"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An unreal past wish uses past perfect for an earlier completed result.</b><br>Correct wording: “I wish the report <b>had been finished</b> before the meeting began.”<br>The passive past perfect matches the later past event.<br>The other options do not establish the counterfactual sequence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): had been finished.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070662","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>Seldom <b>he expresses</b> regret for his decisions. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"does he express"},"2":{"en":"he does express"},"3":{"en":"did he expressed"},"4":{"en":"he expressed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Negative introductory “seldom” requires subject–auxiliary inversion.</b><br>Correct wording: “Seldom <b>does he express</b> regret.”<br>The base verb “express” follows “does.”<br>B and D lack inversion; C uses an invalid past form after “did.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): does he express.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070663","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The legal scholar remarked that the jurisprudential basis for such a ruling, if indeed it existed, appeared to derive more from ideological urgency than from doctrinal consistency. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“If this ruling even has a legal basis, it seems driven more by ideology than jurisprudence,” remarked the scholar."},"2":{"en":"“Does this ruling’s foundation lie in legal tradition, or is it motivated by ideology?” the scholar said."},"3":{"en":"“Surely, no consistent doctrine could justify this ruling—it reeks of urgency,” the scholar observed."},"4":{"en":"“The ruling appears to prioritize ideology over precedent, if legal logic exists at all,” she said."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Preserve the doubtful legal basis and the ideology–doctrine contrast.</b><br>A includes both the conditional “if” and the scholar’s assessment of ideological motivation.<br>B changes the remark into a question.<br>C and D omit or alter key qualifications.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “If this ruling even has a legal basis, it seems driven more by ideology than jurisprudence,” remarked the scholar.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070664","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. The crew loaded the cargo onto the ship.<br>2. The departure was cleared by the harbor master.<br>3. Navigation paths were confirmed.<br>4. The engines were powered up. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-4-3-2"},"2":{"en":"3-4-2-1"},"3":{"en":"4-2-1-3"},"4":{"en":"2-3-1-4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-4-3-2</b><br>The crew loads the cargo and powers up the engines.<br>Navigation paths are then confirmed.<br>The harbor master clears departure last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1-4-3-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070665","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. Results are compiled into dashboards.<br>2. Data is fetched from sources.<br>3. It is cleaned and standardized.<br>4. Analysis is performed. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-3-4-1"},"2":{"en":"1-3-4-2"},"3":{"en":"3-2-4-1"},"4":{"en":"4-3-2-1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-3-4-1</b><br>Data is fetched, cleaned and standardized.<br>Analysis is then performed.<br>The results are compiled into dashboards last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2-3-4-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070666","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. using advanced meteorological models<br>Q. cyclone warnings<br>R. are now issued with greater lead time<br>S. by the national weather bureau [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"SQRP"},"4":{"en":"PRSQ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q supplies the subject, and R the passive predicate.<br>S identifies the issuing authority.<br>P describes the models used.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070667","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. using the real-time demographic dashboard<br>Q. migration patterns during economic downturns<br>R. were mapped by the analytics cell<br>S. for targeted policy interventions [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPRS"},"2":{"en":"QRSP"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"QRPS"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q supplies the subject, and R the passive predicate.<br>S states the policy purpose.<br>P identifies the dashboard used for mapping.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070668","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>Throughout history, the survival of civilizations has hinged less on conquest and more on the ability to preserve and transmit memory. Archives, oral traditions, and artifacts function not merely as records, but as (1)___ of continuity across time. When these are disrupted—through war, colonization, or willful neglect—societies experience not just cultural loss but a rupture in identity. Ironically, modern societies, despite unprecedented access to information, are often more susceptible to (2)___. The speed at which data is consumed renders it disposable; immediacy replaces reflection. In such climates, memory is not erased but drowned—buried under layers of reaction and novelty. Consequently, knowledge ceases to be a cumulative process and becomes a (3)___ one, shaped by urgency rather than inquiry. Institutions meant to safeguard knowledge increasingly function as repositories rather than interlocutors, housing facts without cultivating understanding. The true crisis, then, is not ignorance but a kind of curated (4)___, where forgetting is not accidental but engineered—subtle, continuous, and strategic. Reclaiming memory in such a context requires not nostalgia, but an (5)___ commitment to intergenerational truth-telling.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 1? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"scaffolds"},"2":{"en":"frameworks"},"3":{"en":"templates"},"4":{"en":"vessels"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Vessels (माध्यम) = containers or carriers.</b><br>Archives and artifacts carry continuity across generations.<br>Scaffolds support construction, frameworks provide structure, and templates provide patterns.<br>“Vessels” best expresses the preservation and transmission of memory.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): vessels.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070669","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. under the sovereign green bonds framework<br>Q. were allocated to renewable energy infrastructure<br>R. funds mobilized from the January 2023 issuance<br>S. after alignment with climate action goals [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRPS"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"QSRP"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RQPS</b><br>R supplies the subject: funds from the issuance.<br>Q states their allocation to renewable infrastructure.<br>P identifies the framework, and S the climate-alignment condition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): RQPS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070670","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>Throughout history, the survival of civilizations has hinged less on conquest and more on the ability to preserve and transmit memory. Archives, oral traditions, and artifacts function not merely as records, but as (1)___ of continuity across time. When these are disrupted—through war, colonization, or willful neglect—societies experience not just cultural loss but a rupture in identity. Ironically, modern societies, despite unprecedented access to information, are often more susceptible to (2)___. The speed at which data is consumed renders it disposable; immediacy replaces reflection. In such climates, memory is not erased but drowned—buried under layers of reaction and novelty. Consequently, knowledge ceases to be a cumulative process and becomes a (3)___ one, shaped by urgency rather than inquiry. Institutions meant to safeguard knowledge increasingly function as repositories rather than interlocutors, housing facts without cultivating understanding. The true crisis, then, is not ignorance but a kind of curated (4)___, where forgetting is not accidental but engineered—subtle, continuous, and strategic. Reclaiming memory in such a context requires not nostalgia, but an (5)___ commitment to intergenerational truth-telling.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 2? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"amnesia"},"2":{"en":"relativism"},"3":{"en":"novelty"},"4":{"en":"distraction"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Amnesia (विस्मृति) = loss of memory.</b><br>Information overload makes modern societies susceptible to collective forgetting.<br>Relativism concerns truth, novelty newness, and distraction diverted attention.<br>The passage’s focus on memory makes “amnesia” precise.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): amnesia.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070671","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>Throughout history, the survival of civilizations has hinged less on conquest and more on the ability to preserve and transmit memory. Archives, oral traditions, and artifacts function not merely as records, but as (1)___ of continuity across time. When these are disrupted—through war, colonization, or willful neglect—societies experience not just cultural loss but a rupture in identity. Ironically, modern societies, despite unprecedented access to information, are often more susceptible to (2)___. The speed at which data is consumed renders it disposable; immediacy replaces reflection. In such climates, memory is not erased but drowned—buried under layers of reaction and novelty. Consequently, knowledge ceases to be a cumulative process and becomes a (3)___ one, shaped by urgency rather than inquiry. Institutions meant to safeguard knowledge increasingly function as repositories rather than interlocutors, housing facts without cultivating understanding. The true crisis, then, is not ignorance but a kind of curated (4)___, where forgetting is not accidental but engineered—subtle, continuous, and strategic. Reclaiming memory in such a context requires not nostalgia, but an (5)___ commitment to intergenerational truth-telling.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 3? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"archival"},"2":{"en":"reactive"},"3":{"en":"parallel"},"4":{"en":"empirical"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Reactive (प्रतिक्रियाशील) = driven by immediate responses.</b><br>Knowledge becomes reactive and urgent rather than cumulative and reflective.<br>Archival relates to records, parallel to simultaneity.<br>Empirical means evidence-based.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): reactive.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070672","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>Throughout history, the survival of civilizations has hinged less on conquest and more on the ability to preserve and transmit memory. Archives, oral traditions, and artifacts function not merely as records, but as (1)___ of continuity across time. When these are disrupted—through war, colonization, or willful neglect—societies experience not just cultural loss but a rupture in identity. Ironically, modern societies, despite unprecedented access to information, are often more susceptible to (2)___. The speed at which data is consumed renders it disposable; immediacy replaces reflection. In such climates, memory is not erased but drowned—buried under layers of reaction and novelty. Consequently, knowledge ceases to be a cumulative process and becomes a (3)___ one, shaped by urgency rather than inquiry. Institutions meant to safeguard knowledge increasingly function as repositories rather than interlocutors, housing facts without cultivating understanding. The true crisis, then, is not ignorance but a kind of curated (4)___, where forgetting is not accidental but engineered—subtle, continuous, and strategic. Reclaiming memory in such a context requires not nostalgia, but an (5)___ commitment to intergenerational truth-telling.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 4? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"abstraction"},"2":{"en":"omission"},"3":{"en":"forgetting"},"4":{"en":"obscurity"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Forgetting (भूलना) = loss of retained memory.</b><br>The following clause explicitly describes forgetting as engineered and strategic.<br>Abstraction concerns generalization, omission exclusion.<br>Obscurity means lack of clarity or fame.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): forgetting.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070673","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>Throughout history, the survival of civilizations has hinged less on conquest and more on the ability to preserve and transmit memory. Archives, oral traditions, and artifacts function not merely as records, but as (1)___ of continuity across time. When these are disrupted—through war, colonization, or willful neglect—societies experience not just cultural loss but a rupture in identity. Ironically, modern societies, despite unprecedented access to information, are often more susceptible to (2)___. The speed at which data is consumed renders it disposable; immediacy replaces reflection. In such climates, memory is not erased but drowned—buried under layers of reaction and novelty. Consequently, knowledge ceases to be a cumulative process and becomes a (3)___ one, shaped by urgency rather than inquiry. Institutions meant to safeguard knowledge increasingly function as repositories rather than interlocutors, housing facts without cultivating understanding. The true crisis, then, is not ignorance but a kind of curated (4)___, where forgetting is not accidental but engineered—subtle, continuous, and strategic. Reclaiming memory in such a context requires not nostalgia, but an (5)___ commitment to intergenerational truth-telling.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 5? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"adversarial"},"2":{"en":"unflinching"},"3":{"en":"affective"},"4":{"en":"longitudinal"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Unflinching (अडिग) = resolute and unafraid.</b><br>Intergenerational truth-telling requires an unflinching commitment.<br>Adversarial means hostile, affective emotional.<br>Longitudinal concerns observation over time.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): unflinching.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070674","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P: in producing ethical legal judgments<br>Q: within adversarial frameworks<br>R: judicial discretion<br>S: remains a contentious variable [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RSPQ"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"RPQS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RSPQ</b><br>R supplies the subject and S the predicate.<br>P identifies the area of judgment.<br>Q locates it within adversarial frameworks.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RSPQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070675","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the word that is opposite in meaning to the given word “Murky”. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lucid"},"2":{"en":"Doubtful"},"3":{"en":"Mysterious"},"4":{"en":"Confusing"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Murky (धुंधला) = dark or unclear.</b><br><b>Lucid (स्पष्ट)</b> = clear ✔<br><b>Doubtful (संदिग्ध)</b> = uncertain<br><b>Mysterious (रहस्यमय)</b> = obscure; <b>confusing (भ्रमित)</b> = unclear.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Lucid.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070676","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate homonym to fill in the blank.<br>Hypno Kamalakar created the ___ of a jumping boy on stage. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"illusion"},"2":{"en":"allusion"},"3":{"en":"band"},"4":{"en":"basis"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Illusion (भ्रम) = a false visual impression.</b><br>A stage performer created the illusion of a jumping boy.<br><b>Allusion (संकेत)</b> = indirect reference<br>“Band” and “basis” do not fit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): illusion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070677","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Someone who is skilled at public speaking is called. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Orator"},"2":{"en":"speaker"},"3":{"en":"Messanger"},"4":{"en":"Lecturer"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Orator (वक्ता) = a skilled public speaker.</b><br>A “speaker” speaks but the word does not specifically imply skill.<br>“Messanger” is misspelt and means a carrier of messages.<br>A lecturer delivers instructional talks.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Orator.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070678","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Direction: Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error.<br>If Pushpa Latha have (A)/ passed the law course, (B)/ she would have (C)/ become a lawyer. (D) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"If Pushpa Latha have (A)"},"2":{"en":"passed the law course (B)"},"3":{"en":"she would have (C)"},"4":{"en":"become a lawyer (D)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Third conditional uses “if + subject + had + past participle.”</b><br>Segment A should read “If Pushpa Latha <b>had</b>.”<br>The result “would have become” confirms the unreal past.<br>The other segments are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): If Pushpa Latha have (A).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070679","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate Indirect Speech for the following sentence:<br>The activist said, “People demanded justice.” [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The activist said that people had demanded justice."},"2":{"en":"The activist said that people have been demanded justice."},"3":{"en":"The activist said that people had been demanded justice."},"4":{"en":"The activist said that people has been demanded justice."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past becomes past perfect after a past reporting verb.</b><br>“Demanded” becomes “had demanded.”<br>The other options introduce invalid passive forms or agreement errors.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The activist said that people had demanded justice.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070680","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the INCORRECTLY spelt word. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"prepositionel"},"2":{"en":"seize"},"3":{"en":"sewage"},"4":{"en":"shoulder"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Prepositional (पूर्वसर्ग-संबंधी) = relating to a preposition.</b><br><b>Prepositionel</b> incorrectly uses “e” instead of “a” in the suffix.<br><b>Seize</b> = take hold of; <b>sewage</b> = waste water.<br><b>Shoulder</b> = body part; these are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): prepositionel.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};